          "brief": "What would you do in this situation?\n\n\n### The situation\nPriya has shown you the guest feedback tracker — a shared screen where every complaint or request gets a ticket with a status: OPEN, IN PROGRESS, or CLOSED.\n\nA guest, Ms. Tara Shenoy in Room 308, calls the front desk. She says she reported a broken bedside lamp last night. She was told someone would fix it. Nobody came. She has been sleeping with the room light on. She is tired and not happy.\n\nYou open the tracker and find ticket #1042: 'Broken lamp, Room 308.' Status: CLOSED. Closed at 10:15 pm last night. Notes say: 'Resolved.'\n\nThe lamp is not resolved. Ms. Shenoy is telling you it is not resolved. The ticket says it is.\n\n### Your response\nType: what you say to Ms. Shenoy to settle her down, and what you do with ticket #1042 — do you leave it CLOSED, reopen it, or create a new one? Write the note you would add.",
          "title": "Complaint Already Closed",
          "answer": "typed",
          "easier": "The tracker has a button labelled REOPEN — they only have to decide whether to use it and what to write.",
          "fields": [],
          "harder": "Ms. Shenoy says she wants someone in the room within fifteen minutes or she is leaving a review. They must commit to a realistic timeframe AND fix the record.",
          "minutes": 3,
          "support": "assistant",
          "criteria": [
            "Does not tell Ms. Shenoy the ticket was already closed or use that as a reason to do nothing",
            "Reopens the ticket or flags it as incorrectly closed — does not create a duplicate that buries the first",
            "Writes a note that tells the next person exactly what happened: closed in error, lamp still broken, guest called again"
          ],
          "measures": [
            "Customer care",
            "Clear communication",
            "Follow-through"
          ],
          "needsImage": false
