          "brief": "What would you do in this situation?\n\n\n### The situation\nA guest, Mr. Salim Qureshi, checked out at 7 am — he left his key at the desk, signed the bill, and left. The morning team processed it quickly during a busy breakfast rush. It is now 10 am and you are doing a routine check of the occupancy screen. Room 401 still shows: OCCUPIED — QURESHI, S. Check-out date: tomorrow.\n\nThe room has not been updated. Housekeeping will skip it because the system says it is occupied. If a new guest is given that room tonight, the clean will not have happened.\n\nPriya is at the desk next to you. There is no one asking you to fix this. You noticed it yourself. Type: what you do with the record for Room 401, what you write in the update, and why this matters if you leave it.",
          "title": "Early Check-Out, But the System Says He Is Still Here",
          "answer": "typed",
          "easier": "The system shows a button: MARK AS CHECKED OUT. They decide whether to press it and what to write alongside it.",
          "fields": [],
