          "team": "t1",
          "brief": "What would you do in this situation?\n\n\n### The situation\nYou are at the front desk  at Aranya Grand Hotels. A guest, Mr. Suresh Iyer, checked in last night and has just called the desk. He says his room smells of damp and he could not sleep. He is polite but clearly tired and frustrated. He wants to know what you can do for him.\n\nYou open the AI assistant and type: 'Guest unhappy with room smell, could not sleep, wants compensation or resolution.'\n\nThe assistant produces this draft reply for you to read to Mr. Iyer or send as a message:\n\n---\nDear Mr. Iyer, we sincerely apologise for the inconvenience. We will move you to one of our Premium Suites at no additional charge and offer you a complimentary dinner for two at our rooftop restaurant this evening, as well as a full refund of last night's stay.\n---\n\n### Details to use\nBefore you use this draft, you check the availability screen. It shows:\n- Standard rooms available: 3\n- Deluxe rooms available: 1\n- Premium Suites available: 0\n- Rooftop restaurant: closed on Tuesdays (today is Tuesday)\n\nYour property policy sheet, pinned above the desk, says: room moves require supervisor sign-off, and compensation beyond a complimentary breakfast must be approved by the duty manager.\n\nPriya is at the next desk and can answer quick questions.\n\n### Your response\nWrite the reply you would actually give Mr. Iyer — spoken at the desk or typed as a short message. It must be honest, warm, and not promise anything you cannot deliver right now. Then write two sentences explaining what was wrong with the AI draft and what you changed.",
          "title": "The AI drafted a promise we cannot keep",
          "answer": "typed",
          "easier": "The availability screen is removed; the only error to spot is the closed rooftop restaurant.",
          "fields": [],
