          "brief": "Write what you say to her, from the moment she reaches your counter to the moment she is sorted.\n\n### The situation\nIt's your first morning on the SkyLink Airways check-in floor.\n\nRohan has set you up at Counter 4 and told you to handle walk-up queries while he completes a handover nearby.\n\nA passenger, Mrs. Sunita Ahuja, arrives looking flustered.\n\nShe says she checked in online last night but the boarding pass email never came through.\n\nHer flight — SK 204 to Mumbai — closes in 40 minutes.\n\nShe shows you her phone: the inbox is empty.\n\nYou have a printed quick-reference card on your counter that lists two things staff can do without a supervisor: (1) reprint a boarding pass if the passenger shows a valid photo ID and their booking reference, and (2) direct passengers to the self-service kiosk in Bay 3 for the same.\n\nMrs. Ahuja has her Aadhaar card and her booking reference: SKYAHUJA8802.\n\n### Details to use\nYour job is to help her — calmly, clearly, and quickly — and to leave her feeling looked after, not rushed past.",
