          "brief": "Fill in all five fields exactly as they would appear in the tracker.\n\n### The situation\nHalf an hour into your shift, a passenger at the adjacent counter raised his voice at a ground staff member over a delay.\n\nThe staff member handled it and the passenger has now moved through.\n\nRohan comes over and says: 'Whenever something like that happens, you log it in the Incident Tracker — it's the orange tab on the desktop.\n\nWrite a brief note so the gate team knows what to expect if he shows up there too.' He shows you the tracker for thirty seconds.\n\nThere are five fields: Passenger name, Flight number, Incident type (choose from: verbal dispute / luggage issue / boarding refusal / other), Brief description (two to three sentences), and Status (choose from: resolved / monitoring / escalated).\n\nThe passenger's name, which you saw on the adjacent agent's screen, was Mr. Devraj Sinha.\n\n### Details to use\nHis flight is SK 311 to Delhi, departing in 55 minutes.\n\nThe incident: he objected loudly to a middle seat despite booking economy without a seat selection.\n\nThe agent offered him a seat change at the kiosk; he refused and walked off still unhappy.",
