          "brief": "Write what you say — one short pitch, no more than five sentences, that gives him a reason to say yes without pushing so hard he feels cornered.\n\n### The situation\nIt's day two.\n\nRohan has asked you to stand at Gate 7 for the SK 108 Bengaluru flight while he handles a baggage issue.\n\nBefore leaving, he says: 'We have two business class seats empty.\n\nIf anyone in economy looks like they might bite, offer them the upgrade — it's 2,200 rupees per seat, paid by card at the gate, non-refundable.\n\nDon't pitch everyone, just people who look like they're travelling alone and aren't in a hurry.' A passenger, Mr. Arjun Mehta, walks up a little early.\n\nHe is travelling alone, is relaxed, and mentions unprompted that he has a long day of meetings in Bengaluru tomorrow.\n\nThe flight is two hours and fifteen minutes.\n\nBusiness class on this route includes a wider seat, a meal, and priority disembarkation.\n\nEconomy does not include a meal.\n\nYour job: offer him the upgrade.",
