          "brief": "Write what you say to each of the three passengers — in order — to manage the queue without any of them feeling ignored.\n\n### The situation\nYou are back at Counter 4 on day two.\n\nIt is 6:45 a.m. and the system is running slowly — Rohan tells you it happens most mornings and usually clears in ten minutes.\n\nThree passengers are now in your queue.\n\nPassenger 1: an elderly gentleman who needs a wheelchair.\n\nPassenger 2: a woman travelling with a toddler and a large pram, asking if the pram can be checked at the gate.\n\nPassenger 3: a man in a suit who leans around them and says loudly, 'I have a meeting.\n\nHow long is this going to take?' You can only serve one passenger at a time.\n\nThe wheelchair request goes to a different team — you call it in by pressing the red button under the counter, which pages the mobility assistance crew.\n\nThe pram question you can answer: yes, it can be checked at the gate, and a tag will be put on it there.\n\n### Details to use\nThe man in the suit is just going to have to wait.",
