          "brief": "What would you write or record for this task?\n\n\n### The situation\nOn day three, your supervisor asks you to send a holding message to a passenger, Ms. Priya Nair, whose baggage was offloaded from SK 219 Chennai due to a weight issue on the aircraft. She has already landed. Her bag is still in Bengaluru. You open the AI writing assistant on the SkyLink staff portal and type: 'Write a short apology message to a passenger whose checked bag was not loaded on her flight. We are trying to locate the bag and will send updates.' The assistant returns this draft:\n\n---\nDear Ms. Nair,\n\nWe sincerely apologise for the inconvenience caused. Your bag has been located and will be delivered to your address within 24 hours. Our team is fully committed to making this right, and you will face no further delays.\n\nWarm regards,\nSkyLink Airways Guest Experience Team\n---\n\n### Details to use\nYou have not actually located the bag yet. You do not know the delivery timeline. The 24-hour guarantee does not exist — it is not in any policy you have been given. If you send this and the bag takes three days, you have made a promise SkyLink cannot keep. Fix the draft so it is honest, warm, and still useful to Ms. Nair. Write the corrected message in full.",
