          "id": "t2s027",
          "day": "1",
          "team": "t2",
          "brief": "Look at the numbers.\n\n### The situation\nIt is your first morning at SkyLink Airways. You are shadowing Rohan at the check-in counter when he hands you a printed sheet and says: 'This is the load report for flight SK204 to Hyderabad, departing in ninety minutes. Take a look and tell me if anything looks off.' The sheet shows:\n\nFlight SK204 | Seats: 148 | Check-ins completed: 151 | Boarding passes issued: 144 | Bags checked in: 163 | Bags loaded (per ground team): 158\n\nRohan explains that check-ins completed means passengers who have finished at the counter, and boarding passes issued means passes actually printed and handed over. He adds: 'If those two numbers are more than three apart, we have a problem.'\n\n### Your response\nWrite a short message to Rohan (two to three sentences) saying exactly which figure or figures look wrong, why they are a problem, and what you think should be checked first.",
