          "brief": "What would you write or record for this task?\n\n\n### The situation\nYou work the SkyLink Airways check-in and guest support counter at the airport. It is 11:15 AM. A passenger, Mr Deepak Rao, approaches. His bag was checked in on a SkyLink flight yesterday and arrived with a broken wheel. He filled in a damaged baggage report at the belt last night. He is calm but firm — he wants to know what happens next and roughly how long it takes.\n\nYour process: SkyLink logs the claim, the bag is assessed within 3 working days, and if the damage is confirmed the airline either repairs the bag or pays up to ₹4,000 towards a replacement. Mr Rao will get an SMS update at each stage. Claims rarely exceed 5 working days end to end.\n\n### Details to use\nYou decide to use the AI assistant to draft a quick follow-up SMS to send Mr Rao right now, confirming his claim is logged. You type: 'Draft an SMS to a passenger whose damaged bag claim is now logged. Keep it short.'\n\nThe assistant returns:\n\n---\nDear passenger, your baggage damage claim has been registered. Our team will resolve your issue within 24 hours and contact you shortly. Apologies for the trouble. – SkyLink Airways\n---\n\nThe problem: '24 hours' is not what SkyLink promises. The actual timeline is 3 working days for assessment, up to 5 working days total. Sending '24 hours' to Mr Rao will guarantee a furious follow-up call tomorrow morning when nothing has happened.\n\nMr Rao is still at the counter. Rohan is at the next desk but is on a call and will be free in about two minutes — you do not have time to wait.\n\nDo two things: (1) Write the corrected SMS you will send Mr Rao (keep it under 40 words). (2) In one or two sentences, write what you will say to Mr Rao out loud right now while the SMS is being sent, so he does not leave confused about the timeline.",
          "title": "Wrong Tone, Right Facts",
