          "id": "t3s054",
          "day": "1",
          "team": "t3",
          "brief": "Write the full GuestTrack entry for this return exactly as you would type it.\n\n### The situation\nIt is your first day at the Centurion Mall Group Guest Experience desk. The desk handles returns for stores that are part of the mall's Returns Assistance Programme — guests bring items here instead of going back to the individual store.\n\nEvery return is logged in a paper Return Log and also entered into GuestTrack before the guest leaves. The Return Log is a printed sheet at the desk. A return entry needs: guest name, store name, item description, reason for return, and date.\n\nA guest, Ms. Tripathi, hands you a kurta in a bag. She says she bought it from Aurelia four days ago. The tag is still on. She says it does not fit. She does not have her receipt.\n\n### Details to use\nYou ask the AI assistant how to handle a return without a receipt. It tells you: 'Log the return as normal. In the reason field, write 'No receipt — guest verbal confirmation.' The return is valid under Centurion Mall Group policy as long as the tag is attached and the purchase was within 7 days.'\n\nYou start filling in the Return Log. You write Ms. Tripathi's name, Aurelia, the item, and the reason. When you get to the date of purchase, you pause — she said 'four days ago' but she does not know the exact date.\n\n### Your response\nWhere you do not have a piece of information, show what you write in that field — do not leave it blank and do not guess a date.",
          "title": "The Return That Does Not Quite Fit the Form",
