          "team": "t3",
          "brief": "Rewrite the message so that it is accurate, warm, and does not make promises the ticket does not support.\n\n### The situation\nYou are three days in. The Guest Experience desk sends follow-up messages to guests who logged complaints, once the issue is marked resolved in GuestTrack.\n\nYesterday, a guest named Mr. Okafor reported that the baby changing room on Level 2 was locked during his visit. The ticket — #4501 — was updated by Facilities at 6 p.m.: 'Room unlocked. Key with security desk going forward.' The ticket was marked RESOLVED.\n\nYour supervisor has asked you to send Mr. Okafor a follow-up message by 10 a.m. You ask the AI assistant to draft it. It gives you this:\n\n### Details to use\n---\n'Dear Mr. Okafor, Thank you for bringing the Level 2 baby changing room to our attention. We are happy to confirm that the room is now unlocked and will remain accessible 24 hours a day, every day. Our team has ensured this will not happen again. We look forward to welcoming you back to Centurion Mall. Warm regards, Guest Experience Team'\n---\n\nYou read it. Two things catch your attention. First, the ticket says the key is now with the security desk — it does not say the room is unlocked 24/7. Second, you do not know whether Mr. Okafor was promised anything by the person who took his complaint yesterday.\n\n### Your response\nType the final version you would send.",
