          "brief": "What would you do in this situation?\n\n\n### The situation\nIt is a Saturday afternoon. The mall is busy. There is a queue of four guests at the Guest Experience desk. You are handling them alone — Divya is covering a school group visit at the main atrium and will not be back for forty minutes.\n\nYou are mid-way through logging a complaint from the guest in front of you — Ms. Mehta, who says a parking attendant was rude to her. You have entered her name and contact number into GuestTrack. You have not yet entered the complaint description or set the category. The ticket is sitting open and incomplete.\n\nThe guest behind Ms. Mehta is holding a small child and looks very stressed. She says loudly, 'Excuse me, I just need to know where the nursing room is — it will take two seconds.'\n\n### Details to use\nIf you answer her, Ms. Mehta's open ticket sits unfinished during that time. If you do not answer her, the woman with the child has to wait for a query that genuinely takes ten seconds to answer.\n\n### Your response\nYour task: Decide what you do right now — and then, after both guests are dealt with, type the GuestTrack note for Ms. Mehta's ticket exactly as you would enter it. The note must be complete enough that a colleague could follow up without asking you anything. It is 2:47 p.m.",
