          "brief": "Speak out loud - sixty seconds maximum - what you say to this guest right now, in front of the queue.\n\n### The situation\nIt is Saturday afternoon, your third day. You are at the FastPass collection counter. There are eight guests waiting in line behind the person you are currently serving.\n\nThe guest in front of you, a man in his forties, is speaking loudly: 'I booked FastPass for four rides online. I only see three on this wristband. The fourth one - Galaxy Spin - is not on here. I paid for it. This is completely unacceptable.'\n\nYou can see on the counter tablet that his booking reference shows four rides. But the wristband system shows only three activated. Galaxy Spin is listed as 'pending activation' - which you have never seen before. You do not know how to fix it.\n\nKaran is on a break and will be back in about fifteen minutes.\n\n### Your response\nThen type one sentence about what you do next after you have spoken to him.",
          "title": "Unhappy Guest, Long Line Behind Them",
          "answer": "spoken",
          "easier": "There is no queue behind the guest, so the pressure of eight people watching is removed.",
          "fields": [],
          "harder": "The guest says he is recording the conversation on his phone and will post it online if this is not fixed immediately.",
          "minutes": 4,
          "support": "assistant",
          "criteria": [
            "Acknowledges the problem clearly without blaming the system or making excuses",
            "Does not promise a fix they cannot deliver in the next two minutes",
            "Stays calm and does not raise their voice or match the guest's frustration",
            "The next step is specific: asks the AI assistant how to resolve a 'pending activation' status, or offers to step the guest aside and call Karan, or both - not a vague 'I will sort it out'"
          ],
          "measures": [
            "Customer care",
            "Composure under pressure",
            "Clear communication"
          ],
          "needsImage": false
