          "id": "t4s070",
          "day": "8",
          "team": "t4",
          "brief": "What would you do in this situation?\n\n\n### The situation\nFunSphere India's souvenir kiosk outside Dragon Coaster is your responsibility today. At the start of every shift, the stock sheet is updated with opening counts. At the end of the shift, the closing count is entered. The system then calculates how many units were sold.\n\nHere is the sheet for yesterday's shift:\n\nItem | Opening Stock | Closing Stock | System Says Sold | Actual Guests Served (from POS)\nDragon Coaster Keychain | 80 | 22 | 58 | 58\nFunSphere Cap | 50 | 11 | 39 | 39\nMini Thunder Falls Toy | 60 | 60 | 0 | 0\nPhoto Print Package | 40 | 7 | 33 | 41\nStar Wristband | 30 | 10 | 20 | 20\n\n### Details to use\nOne item shows a mismatch between what the system says was sold and what the point-of-sale (POS) terminal actually recorded. Find it, then write: which item it is, how big the gap is, and two possible reasons the gap might exist. Then say what you would do before restocking that item today.",
          "title": "The Souvenir Stock Sheet",
          "answer": "typed",
          "easier": "Tell the student to look specifically at the last two columns for each item.",
