          "id": "t4s071",
          "day": "15",
          "team": "t4",
          "brief": "What would you say in this situation?\n\n\n### The situation\nIt is midday at FunSphere India. You have just pulled the half-day guest numbers — how many guests entered each zone in the morning — and compared them to what the park typically sees at this time on a Saturday.\n\nHere is what you are looking at:\n\nZone | Today 9 AM–12 PM | Typical Saturday 9 AM–12 PM | Difference\nAdventure Rides | 980 | 950 | +30\nKids' World | 420 | 560 | -140\nFood Court | 670 | 640 | +30\nSpectacle Stage | 110 | 480 | -370\nWater Zone | 890 | 870 | +20\n\nYour team lead has asked you to give a spoken summary — sixty seconds, out loud — covering: which zone has the biggest drop and how serious it is, one likely reason for it, and one practical thing the guest experience team could do right now to improve numbers in that zone before the afternoon rush.\n\n### Details to use\nYou are not expected to know every answer. You are expected to read the data, think it through, and speak clearly. The spoken answer is yours.",
          "title": "Half-Day Guest Numbers That Tell a Story",
