          "brief": "Write the Guest Query note you will type into GuestTrack against booking FSI-20847.\n\n### The situation\nKaran has walked you through the entry desk and shown you how to look up a guest's booking in the system — a tool called GuestTrack. When a ticket is scanned at the turnstile, GuestTrack logs the time, the gate, and marks the ticket 'Admitted'. If a ticket is marked Admitted, it cannot be used again.\n\nA guest, Mr. Suresh Pillai, walks up to your counter. He says he bought a family pass for four people this morning online, but the turnstile just beeped and refused his ticket. You pull up his booking in GuestTrack. The system shows: Booking ID FSI-20847, four-person family pass, purchased at 09:14. Status: ADMITTED — Gate 2 — 09:31.\n\nMr. Pillai says nobody in his family has entered yet. He is getting frustrated. His two children are standing beside him.\n\n### Details to use\nYou cannot override the turnstile yourself — that requires a shift supervisor. What you CAN do right now is: (1) note what the guest has told you, (2) log a 'Guest Query' note inside GuestTrack against his booking, and (3) call the shift supervisor on the desk phone.\n\n### Your response\nThe note must be accurate, complete, and written so the supervisor who reads it knows exactly what to do next — without you having to explain it again.",
