          "brief": "What would you do in this situation?\n\n\n### The situation\nFunSphere India has paid lockers near the main ride zone. When a guest rents a locker, the desk staff assign it in GuestTrack under 'Locker Log' — locker number, guest name, contact number, time out, and time returned. A guest is supposed to be logged as 'returned' the moment they bring the key back.\n\nYou are at the locker desk. A guest, Ms. Ananya Rao, hands you back the key for Locker 14. She says she rented it at 11:00. You open GuestTrack and find Locker 14's log. It reads: Rented 11:00, Guest: Ananya Rao, Contact: 9820-XXXXX, Return: [blank].\n\nSo far so good. But you also notice that Locker 7's row shows: Rented 10:30, Guest: R. Mehta, Return: [blank]. It is now 13:45. Either Mr. Mehta is still using Locker 7, or whoever took that key back forgot to log the return.\n\n### Details to use\nYou need to: (1) close Ms. Rao's record correctly right now, and (2) decide what to do about Locker 7.\n\n### Your response\nWrite two things: the exact text you will type into GuestTrack to close Ms. Rao's log entry, and one or two sentences explaining what you will do about Locker 7 and why — including whether you will update anything in the system before you have confirmed the facts.",
