          "id": "t4s075",
          "day": "3",
          "team": "t4",
          "brief": "What would you write or record for this task?\n\n\n### The situation\nFunSphere India receives guest feedback through an online form. Overnight, a message came in from a guest, Mr. Deepak Verma, who says his son cried the entire ride on the Cyclone because the safety restraint felt loose and the ride operator ignored him when he raised his hand to stop. He is asking for a full refund of his four-ticket family pass (₹3,200) and a written apology.\n\nYour team leader has asked you to draft a reply before the 10 am check-in. You open the AI assistant and paste in Mr. Verma's message with this prompt: 'Write an apology reply from a theme park guest associate to this complaint.'\n\nThe assistant returns this draft:\n\n---\nDear Mr. Verma,\n\n### Details to use\nThank you for writing to us. We are deeply sorry for the distressing experience your family had on the Cyclone. Guest safety is our highest priority and we take all concerns about ride restraints extremely seriously. As a gesture of goodwill, we would like to offer you four complimentary tickets valid for one year, in addition to a full refund of ₹3,200. Please share your bank details and we will process the refund within 24 hours.\n\nWe hope to welcome your family back to FunSphere India soon.\n---\n\nThe actual FunSphere India policy you were given in your induction pack says: Refunds on multi-ticket passes require a written review by the Safety and Guest Relations Manager before any amount is confirmed. No associate may promise a refund amount or timeline in writing to a guest. Complimentary tickets can be offered at supervisor discretion only.\n\nRewrite the reply so it is honest, warm, and consistent with policy. The guest must not feel brushed off, but you cannot confirm the refund amount, the timeline, or the complimentary tickets.",
          "title": "The AI Draft That Promised a Free Ticket",
          "answer": "artefact",
          "easier": "The policy rule about refunds is highlighted in bold in the induction pack excerpt shown to you.",
          "fields": [
            "Revised reply to Mr. Deepak Verma"
          ],
          "harder": "Mr. Verma has added a follow-up message saying he will post about this on social media if he does not hear back within the hour; your reply must also acknowledge this without making it worse.",
          "minutes": 4,
          "support": "assistant",
          "criteria": [
            "The reply removes the specific refund amount (₹3,200), the 24-hour timeline, and the offer of complimentary tickets",
            "The reply acknowledges the safety concern genuinely and does not minimise the son's distress",
            "The reply tells the guest what will happen next — a review — without making a promise the associate cannot keep",
            "The tone stays warm and does not read like a legal disclaimer"
