          "id": "t4s077",
          "day": "18",
          "team": "t4",
          "brief": "What do you do in the system to fix this, in what order, and what do you say to Ms. Sharma while you fix it?\n\n### The situation\nFunSphere India sells 'Rush Pass' upgrades at the guest services counter — these let guests skip the standard queue on five rides. When a guest buys a Rush Pass upgrade at the counter, you are supposed to attach it to their original booking in GuestTrack and mark the booking 'Rush Pass: Active'.\n\nYou sold a Rush Pass this afternoon to a guest, Mr. Farhan Qureshi, Booking ID FSI-31092. It cost ₹600. You processed the payment on the POS machine, then — because there was a queue behind him — you quickly attached the Rush Pass to the booking on screen. Mr. Qureshi went into the park happy.\n\n### Details to use\nAn hour later, a different guest, Ms. Poonam Sharma, Booking FSI-31029, comes to the counter very frustrated. She says she was stopped at the Rush Pass lane and told she does not have a Rush Pass, even though she paid for one. She has her payment receipt showing ₹600.\n\nYou open GuestTrack. FSI-31029 (Ms. Sharma) shows: Rush Pass: Inactive. FSI-31092 (Mr. Qureshi) shows: Rush Pass: Active.\n\nYou look at the booking IDs. 31092 and 31029. You attached the Rush Pass to the wrong record — Mr. Qureshi's — instead of Ms. Sharma's.\n\nKaran is at the next desk.\n\n### Your response\nYou also need to decide: do you log what went wrong, and if so, how do you describe it?",
          "title": "The Upgrade That Went Into the Wrong Record",
          "answer": "typed",
          "easier": "Karan spots the transposed booking IDs immediately and tells you which field to correct first.",
          "fields": [],
          "harder": "Mr. Qureshi has now returned to the counter mid-interaction, asking why his Rush Pass is no longer working — you must handle both guests at once.",
          "minutes": 4,
          "support": "assistant",
          "criteria": [
            "The student corrects both records — removes Rush Pass from FSI-31092 and activates it on FSI-31029 — not just fixes Ms. Sharma's",
