          "brief": "What would you write or record for this task?\n\n\n### The situation\nIt is your thirtieth day. Your team leader, Meena, has given you a project with no further guidance: 'Take a look at last week's complaint data in GuestTrack and tell me what we need to fix. You have until end of shift.'\n\nYou pull up the GuestTrack weekly summary for the past seven days. It shows:\n\nTotal complaints logged: 47\nComplaint categories:\n- Ride wait time: 18\n- Food stall quality: 9\n- Staff behaviour: 6\n- Cleanliness: 7\n- Ticketing / booking errors: 7\n\nComplaints with 'Follow-up completed' status: 29\nComplaints still showing 'Pending': 18\n\nOf the 18 pending:\n- 11 are older than 48 hours\n- 4 are older than 72 hours\n- 3 were logged yesterday\n\nFunSphere India's guest commitment says all complaints receive a follow-up within 48 hours.\n\n### Details to use\nYou also notice the complaint log has a field called 'Root Cause' — which associates are supposed to fill in when they close a complaint. Of the 29 completed complaints, 21 have Root Cause left blank.\n\nMeena is not available to check in. Nobody is checking on you. Write a short note to Meena — as if it is an internal message — that tells her what you found, what is most urgent, and what you think should happen next. You should also say what you are going to do yourself before end of shift.",
          "title": "The Complaint Dashboard Nobody Has Looked At",
