          "day": "2",
          "team": "t4",
          "brief": "What would you do in this situation?\n\n\n### The situation\nIt is 11 a.m.  at FunSphere India. A guest, Mrs. Anita Mehta, walks up to the Guest Experience desk looking upset. She booked a Birthday Bash package for her son's party this afternoon — six children, the Rocket Ranger theme room, a dedicated host, and the special cake. She paid ₹8,400 online three weeks ago.\n\nShe shows you her booking confirmation. The system shows something different: her booking was logged under the wrong date — it shows tomorrow, not today. The Rocket Ranger room is occupied by another party until 4 p.m., and her time slot was 1 p.m. The dedicated party host, Suresh, is already assigned to that other group.\n\nShe is not shouting, but she is close to it. 'Six children are arriving at one o'clock. What are you going to do?'\n\n### Details to use\nYou open the AI assistant and type: 'A guest booked a birthday party for today but the system shows tomorrow. The themed room she paid for is taken. Write a response to calm her down and explain her options.'\n\nThe assistant returns this draft:\n\n---\n'Dear Mrs. Mehta, we sincerely apologise for this mix-up. We will have the Rocket Ranger room ready for you by 1 p.m. as originally planned. Your dedicated host will be with your group throughout. Please be assured that your son's birthday will go ahead exactly as you imagined, and we will also provide a complimentary upgrade to our Deluxe package at no extra charge.'\n---\n\nYou need to respond to Mrs. Mehta in the next two to three minutes. Before you do, read the draft carefully.\n\n### Your response\nYour task: Write the actual response you would give Mrs. Mehta — spoken or written, your choice of format. The response must be honest about what you can and cannot confirm right now, must not repeat any promise the AI made that you cannot keep, and must include at least one concrete thing you will do immediately on her behalf. Do not use the AI draft as written.",
