          "brief": "What would you do in this situation?\n\n\n### The situation\nIt is day 15 at Primus Wealth Bank. Each Relationship Executive tracks their own weekly numbers in a shared spreadsheet. Here is your row for the current week (Monday to Friday, today is Thursday):\n\n| Day | Calls made | Meetings held | Products discussed | Conversions | ₹ value booked (lakh) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Monday | 8 | 2 | 4 | 1 | 3.5 |\n| Tuesday | 9 | 3 | 6 | 2 | 8.0 |\n| Wednesday | 6 | 1 | 2 | 0 | 0 |\n| Thursday | 7 | 2 | 5 | 1 | 4.0 |\n| Friday | – | – | – | – | – |\n| **Week target** | **40** | **12** | **25** | **8** | **30.0** |\n| **Week total so far** | **30** | **8** | **17** | **4** | **15.5** |\n\nThe week target must be met by end of Friday.\n\n### Your response\nWrite a short planning note to yourself (five to seven sentences) that does three things: names which metric is furthest behind relative to what one Friday can realistically recover, explains what Wednesday's row tells you that concerns you, and says what you will do differently on Friday to close the most important gaps. Be specific – name the numbers.",
          "title": "Your weekly target tracker has a gap nobody has flagged",
          "answer": "typed",
          "easier": "Pre-fill the note with the observation about Wednesday and ask the student only to identify the hardest metric to recover and write the Friday plan.",
          "fields": [],
