          "day": "10",
          "team": "t1",
          "brief": "What would you write or record for this task?\n\n\n### The situation\nIt is day 10. A customer, Mr Arun Pillai, sent an email yesterday asking about opening a fixed deposit. He mentioned he needs the money back in exactly five months because he is paying for a family event.\n\nYou asked the AI assistant to draft a reply. Here is what it produced:\n\n---\n*Dear Mr Pillai,*\n\n*Thank you for your interest in Primus Wealth Bank's Fixed Deposit products. We are delighted to confirm that we can offer you a five-month Fixed Deposit at our current rate of 7.8% per annum. You will be able to withdraw the full amount with interest on the exact date you choose, with no penalty.*\n\n*Please visit any branch at your convenience to open the account. A Relationship Executive will be happy to assist you.*\n\n*Warm regards,*\n*Primus Wealth Bank*\n\n---\n\n### Details to use\nYou check the product sheet on your desk. It says:\n- Primus Wealth Bank offers Fixed Deposits for 6 months, 9 months, 12 months, 24 months, and 36 months only. There is no 5-month option.\n- Premature withdrawal is allowed but attracts a 1% penalty on the interest earned.\n- Current rate for 6-month FD: 7.5% p.a.\n\nDo not send the AI draft. Write the correct reply to Mr Pillai yourself – four to six sentences. It should give him accurate information, offer him the closest option that meets his need, and not make any promise the product sheet does not support.",
          "title": "The AI draft promises something you cannot promise",
          "answer": "artefact",
          "easier": "Underline the three errors in the AI draft before showing it to the student, and ask them only to write the corrected reply.",
          "fields": [
            "Your corrected email to Mr Pillai"
