          "brief": "What would you write or record for this task?\n\n\n### The situation\nIt is day 30. Your branch manager has handed you a small project: look at this month's customer contact data for your portfolio and decide where to focus next month's outreach. She says: 'Tell me what you see and what you want to do about it. You have the assistant if you need it. Come back to me by end of day with a one-page plan.'\n\nHere is the data she left with you:\n\n**My portfolio – April contact summary**\n\n| Customer segment | Total customers | Contacted this month | Conversions | Avg ₹ value per conversion (lakh) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Salaried – under 35 | 42 | 38 | 9 | 2.1 |\n| Salaried – 35 to 50 | 55 | 49 | 14 | 5.4 |\n| Salaried – over 50 | 28 | 11 | 3 | 9.2 |\n| Self-employed | 33 | 31 | 8 | 6.7 |\n| Retired | 22 | 6 | 1 | 12.0 |\n\n### Your response\nWrite a one-page plan (roughly 200 words) that does four things: names the segment that has been most under-contacted relative to its size, explains why the data makes that segment worth prioritising despite the low number of calls, proposes two specific actions for next month, and names one thing you will need from the manager or the team to carry out the plan (a resource, approval, or information you do not currently have).",
          "title": "Your segment report shows one customer group nobody is calling",
