          "brief": "Write the call plan you will actually use — three to five bullet points.\n\n### The situation\nYour team leader has booked a 10-minute introductory call for you with Mr Suresh Iyer, a new customer who joined Primus Wealth Bank two weeks ago. All you know is what is in his customer profile on screen: age 34, salaried professional, monthly income about Rs 1.8 lakh, no existing investment products with the bank, has a savings account with a balance of Rs 4.2 lakh sitting idle.\n\nYou want to go into the call prepared, so you ask the AI assistant: 'Give me a short call plan for a first conversation with a 34-year-old salaried customer, Rs 1.8 lakh monthly income, Rs 4.2 lakh idle in savings. Goal is to understand his needs and mention relevant Primus Wealth Bank products.'\n\nThe assistant replies:\n\n### Details to use\n---\nSuggested call plan:\n1. Introduce yourself and thank him for banking with Primus Wealth Bank.\n2. Ask open questions: What are his short and long-term financial goals? Does he have dependants? Is he already investing elsewhere?\n3. Based on his idle balance, suggest: (a) Primus Wealth FD — 7.8% for 12 months; (b) Primus Wealth Flexi RD — Rs 5,000 per month minimum; (c) Primus Wealth Premium Savings Account — waives minimum balance for salaries above Rs 2 lakh.\n4. Close by offering to send a written summary and schedule a follow-up.\n---\n\nYou check the internal product list. Two things stand out:\n- The Flexi RD minimum is Rs 10,000 per month, not Rs 5,000.\n- The Premium Savings Account waiver applies to salaries above Rs 2 lakh. Mr Iyer earns Rs 1.8 lakh, so he does not qualify.\n\nYou have four minutes before the call begins.\n\n### Your response\nFix the errors. Remove any product that does not fit this customer. For each product you keep, write one sentence on why it suits Mr Iyer specifically.",
