          "brief": "What do you do before you close your laptop today?\n\n### The situation\nConnecta Mobile uses a daily dashboard that each executive fills in at the end of the day. It shows: calls made, successful upgrades logged, and revenue added. The numbers feed directly into the team's weekly target report, which the branch manager reviews every Monday.\n\nAt the end of today you open your dashboard row. Here is what it shows:\n\nCalls made: 18 | Upgrades logged in CRM: 3 | Dashboard figure you entered yesterday: 4 upgrades\n\nYou stop. Yesterday you entered 4 upgrades. But when you check the CRM call logs from yesterday, you can only find 3 completed upgrade records. The fourth one — a customer named Mr. Farhan — you remember now: he said 'yes' on the call, but when you sent the confirmation SMS, it bounced. You logged him as an upgrade in the dashboard but never completed the CRM record because the SMS issue distracted you.\n\n### Details to use\nSneeha is at her desk. The Monday report goes to the manager tomorrow morning.",
          "title": "The Dashboard Number That Does Not Match the Call Log",
          "answer": "typed",
          "easier": "The manager is on leave — the Monday report is delayed by two days. Does that change what you do today?",
          "fields": [],
