          "id": "t2s036",
          "day": "15",
          "team": "t2",
          "brief": "What do you do before you send anything?\n\n### The situation\nYou are following up with a customer, Mr. Prashant Tiwari, who complained four days ago that his data speed had dropped and he was not informed before his plan changed. He is an unhappy customer and a potential churn risk — meaning he might leave Connecta Mobile.\n\nYou ask the AI assistant to draft a follow-up email to send him. You give it this prompt: 'Draft a follow-up email to an unhappy customer about a data speed complaint. Professional and warm tone.'\n\nThe assistant returns this draft:\n\n---\nDear Mr. Tiwari,\n\nThank you for raising your concern with us. We sincerely apologise for the disruption to your service. Our team has reviewed your account and I am pleased to confirm that your original plan settings have been restored and your data speed is now back to normal.\n\n### Details to use\nAs a goodwill gesture, we will be adding 5GB of free data to your account within 24 hours.\n\nPlease do not hesitate to reach out if you need anything further.\n\nWarm regards,\nConnecta Mobile Customer Team\n---\n\nYou check Mr. Tiwari's CRM record. It shows: 'Data complaint raised Day 1. Tech team acknowledged Day 2. Resolution: pending — no update since.' There is no record of his plan being restored. There is no approval on file for a free data credit.\n\nSneeha is at her desk.",
          "title": "AI Draft, Wrong Commitment",
          "answer": "typed",
          "easier": "The two problems are pointed out — you only need to rewrite the email correctly.",
          "fields": [],
          "harder": "Rewrite the full email yourself, without the assistant, in a way that is still warm and does not make either false promise.",
          "minutes": 4,
          "support": "assistant",
          "criteria": [
            "Identifies that the draft claims the issue is resolved when the CRM shows it is still pending",
            "Identifies that the 5GB credit is promised without any approval on file",
