          "day": "1",
          "team": "t3",
          "brief": "What would you do in this situation?\n\n\n### The situation\nIt is your first afternoon at Suraksha Life Insurance. Arjun, the colleague sitting next to you, has shown you the team's shared policy tracker. Each row is a customer who has recently bought a policy. The tracker has four columns: customer name, policy type, premium amount (monthly, in rupees), and status.\n\nArjun asks you to read through five rows and check whether the status column matches what is written in the notes column just next to it. He says: 'The notes are typed in by whoever did the welcome call. Sometimes the status does not get updated to match.'\n\nHere are the five rows:\n\n### Details to use\n| Customer | Policy type | Monthly premium (₹) | Status | Welcome call note |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Mrs Iyer | Term Life | 2,400 | Active | 'Welcome call done, customer happy, policy live' |\n| Mr Fernandes | Health Rider | 1,100 | Pending | 'Customer asked to call back next week, not yet confirmed' |\n| Ms Chauhan | Term Life | 3,200 | Active | 'Customer said she never received the policy document, call dropped' |\n| Mr Pillai | Child Plan | 1,800 | Active | 'Policy cancelled at customer request on 14th' |\n| Ms Rathi | Health Rider | 950 | Pending | 'Welcome call done, all documents submitted, policy confirmed live' |\n\nTwo rows have a mismatch between the status and the note. Write down which two they are and, for each one, say in one sentence what the correct status should be and why.",
          "title": "The policy tracker says one thing, the welcome call notes say another",
          "answer": "typed",
          "easier": "Tell the student there are exactly two mismatches and that they involve the status column not matching what the note says happened.",
          "fields": [],
          "harder": "Add a sixth row where the mismatch is subtle — status says Active, note says 'premium not yet realised, follow-up due' — and ask the student to rank all mismatches by urgency.",
          "minutes": 4,
