          "brief": "What would you do in this situation?\n\n\n### The situation\nIt is day two. Arjun hands you a printed renewal follow-up list — these are existing Suraksha Life Insurance customers whose policies are due for renewal soon. Your job this morning is to call each one and remind them to renew. Arjun says: 'Before you start calling, just scan the list. Sometimes there are entries that should not be there.'\n\nHere is the list:\n\n| Customer | Policy number | Renewal due date | Premium due (₹) | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Mr Hegde | SL-10042 | 15 June | 4,800 | No previous contact issues |\n| Mrs Bose | SL-10078 | 18 June | 2,200 | Requested morning calls only |\n| Mr Tiwari | SL-10091 | 10 June | 3,500 | — |\n| Ms Anand | SL-10055 | 22 June | 1,950 | Policy lapsed 3 months ago, not renewed |\n| Mr Desai | SL-10033 | 19 June | 5,100 | No previous contact issues |\n\nToday's date is 12 June.\n\n### Your response\nWrite two things: (1) which entry should not be on a renewal call list and why, and (2) one sentence about what you would do with that entry before starting calls.",
