          "brief": "What would you write or record for this task?\n\n\n### The situation\nA customer, Mr Nair, called this morning asking about the Suraksha Shield term plan. You took notes during the call. Now you need to send him a short follow-up email summarising what you discussed.\n\nYour notes say:\n- Policy term: 20 years\n- Sum assured: ₹50 lakh\n- Monthly premium quoted: ₹1,850\n- Free-look period: 15 days (this is Suraksha's standard policy)\n- Mr Nair said he wants to discuss with his wife before deciding\n\nYou use the AI assistant to draft the email. Here is what it produces:\n\n---\nDear Mr Nair,\n\nThank you for speaking with us today about the Suraksha Shield term plan.\n\nAs discussed, here is a summary of what we covered:\n- Policy term: 20 years\n- Sum assured: ₹50 lakh\n- Monthly premium: ₹1,650\n- Free-look period: 30 days — you can cancel and get a full refund within this window\n\n### Details to use\nPlease take your time to discuss with your family. I am happy to answer any questions.\n\nWarm regards,\nSuraksha Life Insurance\n---\n\nBefore you send this, read it carefully against your notes. There are two things in the draft that do not match what you recorded. Find them, then write the corrected email — fixing only the errors, keeping everything else exactly as the AI wrote it.",
