          "team": "t4",
          "brief": "Write the message you will actually send Meena.\n\n### The situation\nYou are a Relationship Executive, which means you speak to customers about small loans, explain what they qualify for, and help them apply. Your manager has set up an AI writing assistant on your laptop and told you to use it for customer messages.\n\nA customer named Meena Pillai called yesterday and left a message asking whether she can get a top-up loan of ₹25,000 on her existing account. Her current loan balance is ₹8,400 and she has never missed a payment. You need to send her a WhatsApp message today to keep her warm while her eligibility is checked by the credit team — that check takes 2 to 3 working days.\n\nYou ask the AI assistant to draft the message. It produces this:\n\n### Details to use\n---\n\"Dear Meena ji, thank you for your loyalty to Sahayog Finserve! We are happy to confirm that you are eligible for a top-up loan of ₹25,000. Please visit our branch with your Aadhaar card and we will process it for you today itself. Looking forward to seeing you!\"\n---\n\nRead the draft carefully. There is at least one thing in it that Sahayog Finserve cannot actually stand behind yet — the credit check has not happened. If you send this message and Meena arrives at the branch today, what happens?\n\n### Your response\nIt should keep her interested, be honest about where things are, tell her the next step and when to expect it, and sound warm but professional. Do not copy the AI draft. Fix what is wrong.",
