          "brief": "What would you do in this situation?\n\n\n### The situation\nAt ZoomBasket, every delivery problem gets logged as a ticket in the hub system. Each ticket has a status: Open, In Progress, or Closed. It also shows who last updated it and when.\n\nPriya has asked you to look at this morning's open ticket list and tell her which one worries you most and why. Here is the list as it stands at 9 a.m.:\n\n### Details to use\n| Ticket ID | Issue | Status | Last updated | Updated by |\n|-----------|-------|--------|-------------|------------|\n| TK-441 | Customer says order never arrived — 6 p.m. slot yesterday | Open | Yesterday 6:42 p.m. | Rider R. Singh |\n| TK-442 | Bag seal broken on delivery — customer complaint | In Progress | Today 8:10 a.m. | Ops team |\n| TK-443 | Wrong items in order — customer requesting replacement | Open | Yesterday 2:15 p.m. | Rider A. Khan |\n| TK-444 | Rider reported unsafe building entrance — no lift, 6th floor | Open | Yesterday 11:03 a.m. | Rider S. Nair |\n| TK-445 | App shows delivered but customer says not received | Open | Today 8:55 a.m. | System auto |\n\nIt is now 9 a.m. Write two to three sentences: which ticket concerns you most, your specific reason based on what the list actually shows, and one action you would suggest Priya take on it today.",
          "title": "Ticket list — what has nobody touched?",
          "answer": "typed",
          "easier": "Ask only: which ticket has gone the longest without a human update, and how long has it been?",
          "fields": [],
          "harder": "Add a sixth ticket — TK-446, logged three minutes ago, rider reports a road closure affecting four live deliveries — and ask how the priority order changes.",
          "minutes": 3,
          "support": "assistant",
          "criteria": [
            "Selects TK-443 or TK-444 as most concerning — TK-443 because a replacement has been neither arranged nor updated since 2:15 p.m. yesterday (nearly 19 hours), TK-444 because it is a safety report with no follow-up for over 22 hours; either is a defensible answer if the reasoning uses the timestamps",
            "Reasoning is grounded in specific data from the table (time gap, status, who updated it) rather than a general claim that it 'looks bad'",
            "Suggested action is concrete and within a supervisor's scope — contact the customer, reassign the ticket, escalate the safety issue — not vague",
            "Does not confuse which ticket is TK-445 (system-auto, this morning) with the older unresolved ones"
          ],
          "measures": [
            "Problem solving",
            "Planning and organising",
            "Clear communication"
