          "brief": "What would you write or record for this task?\n\n\n### The situation\nIt is day three. You have been asked to send a brief end-of-day summary to the hub's operations group chat. The format is standard: total orders, delivery rate, and any issues to flag.\n\nHere are today's actual figures:\n\n| Slot | Assigned | Delivered | Failed |\n|------|----------|-----------|--------|\n| 8–10 a.m. | 40 | 40 | 0 |\n| 10–12 p.m. | 44 | 43 | 1 |\n| 12–2 p.m. | 48 | 46 | 2 |\n| 2–4 p.m. | 51 | 51 | 0 |\n| 4–6 p.m. | 43 | 42 | 1 |\n| 6–8 p.m. | 46 | 44 | 2 |\n\nYou asked the AI assistant to draft the message. It produced this:\n\n---\n*'ZoomBasket Hub — End of Day Summary. Total orders: 272. Delivered: 268. Failed: 4. Delivery rate: 98.5%. No major issues to flag. Good day overall.'*\n\n---\n\n### Details to use\nRead the draft against the table. Write the corrected message yourself — same short format, accurate numbers. Then add one sentence below the message explaining what the AI got wrong and how you caught it.\n\nDo not send the draft as-is.",
          "title": "The AI draft gets the numbers wrong",
          "answer": "artefact",
          "easier": "Tell the student in advance that the draft contains at least one number error and ask them to find and fix it.",
          "fields": [
