          "brief": "Speak your answer out loud — sixty seconds, as if you are standing at your manager's desk.\n\n### The situation\nIt is the 15th of the month. Your manager has asked you to look at the first two weeks of hub throughput data and come back in ten minutes with: the one day that looks most out of line, what the numbers actually show, and what you would check to understand why.\n\nHere is the daily summary for days 1–14:\n\n### Details to use\n| Day | Orders assigned | Delivered | Failed | Delivery rate |\n|-----|----------------|-----------|--------|---------------|\n| 1 | 258 | 252 | 6 | 97.7% |\n| 2 | 261 | 254 | 7 | 97.3% |\n| 3 | 255 | 251 | 4 | 98.4% |\n| 4 | 270 | 264 | 6 | 97.8% |\n| 5 | 249 | 244 | 5 | 98.0% |\n| 6 | 268 | 262 | 6 | 97.8% |\n| 7 | 271 | 265 | 6 | 97.8% |\n| 8 | 265 | 258 | 7 | 97.4% |\n| 9 | 263 | 256 | 7 | 97.3% |\n| 10 | 260 | 253 | 7 | 97.3% |\n| 11 | 274 | 249 | 25 | 90.9% |\n| 12 | 269 | 263 | 6 | 97.8% |\n| 13 | 257 | 251 | 5 | 97.7% |\n| 14 | 262 | 256 | 6 | 97.7% |\n\n### Your response\nName the day, say what the numbers show compared to the rest of the fortnight, and give two specific things you would look at to understand what happened. Do not read the table aloud — talk about what it means.",
