          "team": "t2",
          "brief": "Write your one-page summary.\n\n### The situation\nIt is day thirty. You are now expected to run the hub's weekly slot planning without someone checking your work first.\n\nYou have been handed this week's slot-level delivery data and told: 'Use this to plan next week's rider allocation. Tell me which slots need more cover, which are over-resourced, and what you are going to do about it. I need a one-page summary by end of day.'\n\nThis week's data (riders on shift vs orders delivered per slot, Monday–Friday average):\n\n### Details to use\n| Slot | Avg riders on shift | Avg orders delivered | Avg failed | Notes |\n|------|--------------------|--------------------|------------|-------|\n| 8–10 a.m. | 6 | 38 | 1 | — |\n| 10–12 p.m. | 6 | 41 | 1 | — |\n| 12–2 p.m. | 8 | 52 | 1 | — |\n| 2–4 p.m. | 8 | 49 | 6 | 3 riders called off twice this week |\n| 4–6 p.m. | 6 | 44 | 5 | High failure — cause not yet confirmed |\n| 6–8 p.m. | 10 | 48 | 2 | — |\n\nWeekend data (Saturday–Sunday average):\n\n| Slot | Avg riders on shift | Avg orders delivered | Avg failed |\n|------|--------------------|--------------------|------------|\n| 12–2 p.m. | 6 | 61 | 8 |\n| 4–6 p.m. | 6 | 59 | 9 |\n| 6–8 p.m. | 8 | 62 | 3 |\n\n### Your response\nIt should: name the two or three slots most in need of attention next week, explain what the data shows for each one, say what you plan to do (rider reallocation, investigation, or escalation as appropriate), and flag anything you cannot resolve without more information. You do not have an unlimited roster — if you add cover to one slot, say where you are taking it from.",
          "title": "Build next week's slot plan from this week's gaps",
