          "brief": "What would you do in this situation?\n\n\n### The situation\nYou are on your second morning at ZoomBasket Logistics. your teammate Priya is showing you the hub's dispatch tracker — a screen that lists every order, its current status, and which rider picked it up. One row catches your eye:\n\nOrder #ZB-00441 | Customer: Meera Sinha | Status: DELIVERED | Rider: Kiran | Time marked: 07:14\n\nBut Order #ZB-00441 is physically sitting in Bay 3, right in front of you. The bag is sealed and tagged. It has not moved. Kiran has already left for his next run.\n\nPriya explains that the tracker is the official record ZoomBasket uses when customers raise complaints and when riders are reviewed. If it says DELIVERED, the system will auto-close the ticket at noon and no follow-up will be triggered.\n\n### Details to use\nYou have two things to do before noon:\n1. Fix the record so it reflects reality.\n2. Make sure the order still reaches the customer today.\n\n### Your response\nType out exactly what you would update in the tracker — what status you would change it to, what note you would add so the next person can pick this up, and what you would do about the order itself. You cannot reach Kiran right now. Priya is at her desk if you need her.",
