          "id": "t2s026",
          "day": "30",
          "team": "t2",
          "brief": "Write your one-page plan for Ritika.\n\n### The situation\nThe hub manager at ZoomBasket Logistics, Ritika, has handed you your first solo project. She says:\n\n'We had three customer escalations last month where our system record said one thing and the actual situation was something else. Refund promised but not processed, order marked delivered but sitting in the bay, attendance showing six riders when we had four. Each one created a bigger problem than the original mistake. I want you to figure out where the gaps are and give me a one-page plan by Friday.'\n\nRitika is in meetings all day. You are on your own.\n\nBelow is the data she left you — a table of the 12 tickets escalated to her in the past 30 days, with the reason each was escalated:\n\n### Details to use\nTicket | Reason escalated\nZB-T-3301 | System showed DELIVERED, order was in hub\nZB-T-3318 | Refund logged by rider as 'processed', never submitted to finance\nZB-T-3325 | Attendance sheet showed 6, hub had 4 — over-capacity routed\nZB-T-3340 | Damage logged as INTACT, customer complained, no auto-refund triggered\nZB-T-3355 | Order marked DELIVERED at 6 am before rider left hub\nZB-T-3367 | Rider logged return as completed, bag never scanned back in\nZB-T-3381 | Refund logged by rider as 'processed', never submitted to finance\nZB-T-3390 | Attendance sheet showed 5, hub had 3\nZB-T-3402 | System showed DELIVERED, order was in hub\nZB-T-3415 | Damage logged as INTACT, customer complained, no auto-refund triggered\nZB-T-3428 | Refund logged by rider as 'processed', never submitted to finance\nZB-T-3441 | Order marked DELIVERED before rider left hub\n\n### Your response\nIt should name the patterns you see in the data, say which gap is causing the most harm, and give two or three specific actions the hub can take — not general advice, but things someone can actually do on Monday morning. Say what you need from Ritika to make those actions happen.",
