          "day": "3",
          "team": "t2",
          "brief": "What would you do in this situation?\n\n\n### The situation\nIt is 6:50 am on day three. Your hub opens at 7:00 am and runs two overlapping shift slots: Slot A (7 am–1 pm, needs 4 sorters) and Slot B (11 am–5 pm, needs 4 sorters). The shift roster on the whiteboard reads:\n\nSlot A confirmed: Dinesh, Meera, Farhan, Pooja\nSlot B confirmed: Rajan, Shalini, Thomas\nSlot B — fourth position: OPEN (Nandini called in sick at 6:30 am)\n\nPriya, the senior hub associate at the next desk, is on a call with the dispatch team and will be free in about ten minutes. You type into the assistant: 'I need to cover a missing sorter for Slot B, 11 am to 5 pm today at a food delivery hub. What should I do?'\n\nThe assistant replies:\n\n### Details to use\n---\n'Here are your options in order of speed:\n1. Offer the open slot to a Slot A sorter willing to extend their shift by four hours (11 am–5 pm overlap). Check who is free.\n2. Call your standby or on-call list if your hub maintains one.\n3. Redistribute Slot B work across the three confirmed sorters temporarily — a 25% increase in load per person is within normal range for short gaps.\n4. Contact your staffing agency for a same-day replacement.\nRecommend starting with option 1 as it is the fastest.'\n---\n\nThe assistant's response is mostly sensible but one of its four options contains a figure that could cause a real problem if you act on it without checking. Identify which option has the questionable figure, explain in one sentence why it is a risk here, and then write the two steps you would actually take first — in order — to cover the Slot B gap before 11 am.",
