          "day": "1",
          "team": "t3",
          "brief": "Look at those five numbers.\n\n### The situation\nYour manager, Priya, has handed you a printed sheet and asked you to do a simple check before the 9 AM sort begins. The sheet is the morning bay count — how many parcels were logged into each bay overnight by the night crew.\n\nThe sheet shows:\n- Bay 1: 142 parcels\n- Bay 2: 98 parcels\n- Bay 3: 211 parcels\n- Bay 4: 57 parcels\n- Bay 5: 0 parcels\n\nTotal on sheet: 508\n\nArVind, the colleague at the next desk, points at the screen and says: 'The system total for last night is 534. If you spot anything odd on the sheet, just flag it to Priya — she'll want to know before the sort starts.'\n\n### Your response\nOne of them does not look right given the others, and the sheet total does not match the system. Write a short note to Priya — two or three sentences — saying what you found, which bay you think needs a recheck, and why.",
          "title": "The Bay Count Does Not Match",
          "answer": "typed",
          "easier": "Tell the student the gap is 26 and ask them only to say which bay to recheck and why.",
          "fields": [],
          "harder": "Remove Arvind's hint. The student must notice the mismatch between sheet and system without being told the system figure — give only the sheet and ask what they would do next.",
          "minutes": 3,
          "support": "assistant",
          "criteria": [
            "Identifies that the sheet total (508) does not match the system total (534), a gap of 26",
            "Flags Bay 5 as the most likely place to recheck, since zero parcels overnight is unusual",
            "Does not guess or invent a cause — asks for a recheck rather than stating what happened",
            "Note is short enough that Priya can read it in under thirty seconds"
          ],
          "measures": [
            "Problem solving",
            "Clear communication"
          ],
          "needsImage": false
