          "id": "t4s054",
          "day": "1",
          "team": "t4",
          "brief": "Look at the numbers, decide what needs a comment, and write the comment you would actually put in the shift log.\n\n### The situation\nIt is 8:15  at ConnectCore Supply Chain. You are a Hub Supervisor trainee, shadowing the opening shift. The hub dispatcher has handed you a printed sheet called the Daily Throughput Log. It shows how many parcels each bay processed in yesterday's full shift.\n\nThe sheet reads:\n\nBay 1 — 214 parcels dispatched\nBay 2 — 198 parcels dispatched\nBay 3 — 201 parcels dispatched\nBay 4 — 47 parcels dispatched\nBay 5 — 209 parcels dispatched\n\nThe dispatcher tells you: 'Each bay runs the same belt configuration. Target is 190 to 220 parcels per shift. Anything outside that range needs a supervisor comment in the shift log before the morning briefing.'\n\nThe shift log is a simple notebook on the desk. The morning briefing is in ten minutes.\n\n### Your response\nBe specific — name the bay, the number, and what you think the next step should be.",
          "title": "Morning Throughput Sheet",
          "answer": "artefact",
          "easier": "The target range is written on the sheet itself, so no mental calculation is needed.",
          "fields": [
            "Your shift log comment"
          ],
          "harder": "Add a Bay 6 row showing 231 parcels and ask whether that also needs a comment and why.",
          "minutes": 3,
          "support": "assistant",
          "criteria": [
            "Identifies Bay 4 (47 parcels) as the only figure outside the target range",
            "Does not flag bays that are within range",
            "States a concrete next step, such as checking the belt, reviewing maintenance records, or asking the bay operator",
            "Comment is short enough to be written in a notebook, not a report"
          ],
          "measures": [
            "Planning and organising",
            "Problem solving",
            "Clear communication"
          ],
          "needsImage": false
