          "id": "t4s055",
          "day": "2",
          "team": "t4",
          "brief": "Look at the sheet.\n\n### The situation\nMeena, the experienced hub supervisor at the next desk, has given you a stock sheet to review before the afternoon delivery arrives. ConnectCore Supply Chain handles telecom equipment, and certain items are tracked carefully because they are high-value.\n\nThe stock sheet shows what the system says should be on the shelves right now:\n\nFibre splice trays — system says 60, counted by bay staff this morning: 60\nRJ45 patch panels (24-port) — system says 48, counted: 48\nCable management brackets — system says 200, counted: 183\nOptical fibre rolls (50m) — system says 30, counted: 30\nDIN rail mounting kits — system says 75, counted: 75\n\n### Details to use\nMeena says: 'The system count and the physical count should match. If they do not, you log a discrepancy note in the stock tracker — item name, both numbers, and whether we need to hold that item's outbound orders until we investigate. Discrepancies of five or fewer could be a counting error. More than five and we treat it as a real gap.'\n\n### Your response\nWrite the discrepancy note you would enter into the stock tracker.",
          "title": "Equipment Stock Sheet Discrepancy",
          "answer": "artefact",
          "easier": "The gap size threshold is stated as a rule, so the decision is straightforward arithmetic.",
          "fields": [
            "Your discrepancy note for the stock tracker"
          ],
          "harder": "Add a second discrepancy: optical fibre rolls counted at 27 instead of 30 (gap of 3), and ask what is different about how you handle that one.",
          "minutes": 3,
          "support": "assistant",
          "criteria": [
            "Identifies cable management brackets as the only item with a gap (system 200, counted 183, gap of 17)",
            "States both figures (system and physical count) in the note",
            "Recommends holding outbound orders for that item pending investigation, consistent with the rule given",
            "Does not flag items where the counts match"
          ],
          "measures": [
            "Planning and organising",
            "Follow-through",
            "Clear communication"
          ],
          "needsImage": false
        },
