          "brief": "without asking anyone, read the list and decide which ticket you would act on first.\n\n### The situation\nYou have been given access to the hub's escalation tracker for the first time. The tracker is a simple table where any staff member can raise an issue that needs a supervisor to act on it. Open tickets stay on the list until a supervisor closes them.\n\nHere is what the tracker shows right now:\n\nTicket 101 — Raised: today 07:10 — 'Bay 3 belt making grinding noise' — Status: Open\nTicket 98 — Raised: yesterday 14:30 — 'Pallet of fibre rolls blocking emergency exit, Bay 2' — Status: Open\nTicket 95 — Raised: three days ago 09:00 — 'Vending machine in staff room empty' — Status: Open\nTicket 103 — Raised: today 08:50 — 'Driver waiting — POD system not printing, cannot dispatch' — Status: Open\nTicket 99 — Raised: yesterday 17:00 — 'Overtime hours for last Tuesday not yet approved' — Status: Open\n\n### Your response\nWrite two to three sentences explaining which ticket you chose, why, and what you would do in the next five minutes.",
