          "brief": "What would you do in this situation?\n\n\n### The situation\nIt is end of day seven. The hub runs a simple dashboard that the dispatch team updates throughout the shift. You are reviewing today's numbers before signing off the shift report.\n\nThe dashboard shows:\n\nParcels received into hub today: 1,040\nParcels dispatched to drivers today: 870\nParcels held for re-attempt tomorrow: 95\nParcels returned to sender today: 42\nParcels currently on shelves (closing count): 61\n\nThe rule you have been taught: Received = Dispatched + Held + Returned + Closing count. If the numbers do not balance, do not sign off the shift report until you know why.\n\nCheck the numbers. Write the note you would add to the shift report — state whether it balances, and if not, what the gap is and what you are doing before you sign off.",
