          "brief": "Write the findings note you will read at Monday's briefing.\n\n### The situation\nIt is day thirty. Your manager has handed you a week's worth of bay throughput data and asked you to present a short findings note at Monday's team briefing. No one will check your work before the meeting. You need to say what the numbers show, what the problem is, and what you recommend.\n\nHere is the data — parcels dispatched per bay per day, Monday to Friday:\n\nMon   Tue   Wed   Thu   Fri\nBay 1:    212   209   211   210   208\nBay 2:    201   198   203   199   200\nBay 3:    215   211   214   212   210\nBay 4:    205   198   196   84    81\nBay 5:    209   207   208   205   203\n\nTarget per bay per shift: 190–220.\nA bay that falls below 190 on two or more consecutive days is flagged for maintenance review under the hub's Standard Operating Procedure.\n\n### Your response\nIt should: name the bay with the problem, state when the drop started, say whether the SOP threshold has been triggered, and give one specific recommendation. Keep it under 120 words.",
