          "brief": "Write the update you add to ticket HD-2247 right now, before you log off.\n\n### The situation\nConnectCore Supply Chain runs a ticket system called HubDesk. Every customer escalation — wrong item, damaged goods, late delivery — gets a ticket. You have been shown that tickets must be updated the moment any action is taken, so the next person can see exactly where things stand.\n\nIt is 4 p.m. on a Friday. You took a call at 2 p.m. from a site engineer in Hyderabad: his order, ticket HD-2247, was for 40 fibre splice trays but only 32 arrived. You checked the outbound photo log and found the shortfall was a packing error on your hub's side. You promised him you would raise a replacement for 8 trays before end of day. You raised the replacement order at 2:45 p.m. — replacement order number REP-0093 — but you got pulled into a shift meeting and never updated ticket HD-2247.\n\n### Details to use\nIt is now 4:55 p.m. You have five minutes before the shift ends and you are tired. The outgoing night supervisor, Priya, will inherit open tickets at 5 p.m. Ticket HD-2247 still shows status 'Open – Awaiting Investigation'. The notes field has nothing after your 2 p.m. entry that says 'Customer called. Checking stock photo.'",
          "title": "Fix it later becomes fix it never",
