          "brief": "What would you do in this situation?\n\n\n### The situation\nYou are doing a mid-morning stock check at ConnectCore Supply Chain. You scan the cable drum bay. The hub's inventory system, StockTrack, shows this for Bay C-7:\n\nItem: CAT6A shielded cable drum (500m) | System count: 14 | Status: All available\n\nYou count the physical shelf. There are 11 drums.\n\nYou ask the morning loader, Deepak, whether any went out today. He checks his sheet and says three drums went on the 8 a.m. van to a tower site in Pune — dispatch order DS-5502 — but he forgot to scan them out because the scanner battery died and he was in a hurry. The system was never updated.\n\nDeepak says: 'I'll sort it later, don't worry about it.' He is already heading to another bay.\n\n### Details to use\nStockTrack has a 'Manual Adjustment' function that requires a reason code and a note. Leaving it uncorrected means the system will show 14 units available and the sales team may commit stock that does not exist.\n\nDescribe what you do in the next five minutes — what you enter in StockTrack, what reason code or notes you use, and whether you do anything else.",
