          "brief": "What would you write or record for this task?\n\n\n### The situation\nA customer — Ravi Nair, procurement lead at a telecom contractor — has sent an angry email. His order, CON-9104, for 6 optical fibre splice closures arrived with 2 units visibly cracked. He wants to know what happened and what you will do about it.\n\nYou open the AI assistant and type: 'Write a reply to a customer whose two splice closures arrived cracked. We will replace them.'\n\nThe assistant returns this draft:\n\n---\nDear Ravi,\nThank you for reaching out. We sincerely apologise for the inconvenience. We have investigated the matter and are pleased to confirm that two replacement units will be dispatched to you within 24 hours. Your satisfaction is our priority and we assure you this will not happen again.\nWarm regards,\nConnectCore Supply Chain\n---\n\n### Details to use\nYou check the actual situation in HubDesk and StockTrack:\n- Ticket HD-2301 is open. Root cause is not yet confirmed — the loading photo shows the units were intact at dispatch, so damage likely occurred in transit.\n- You have 4 splice closures in stock at your hub, so replacements can go out — but the courier has not been booked yet, so 24-hour dispatch is not confirmed.\n- You have no authority to promise 'this will not happen again' for a courier-side issue.\n\nDo you send the draft, edit it, or write something different? Produce the email you actually send to Ravi Nair.",
