          "brief": "Decide: will you send this message, edit it, or scrap it entirely?\n\n### The situation\nIt is 8:45 a.m.  at ConnectCore Supply Chain's delivery hub. You supervise the morning shift, which moves telecom equipment — routers, fibre spools, antenna mounts — out to installation sites across the region.\n\nA site coordinator named Arjun has emailed in: his team is waiting at a tower site in Pune and the fibre spool consignment (Order #FC-2291) has not arrived. The hub tracker shows the consignment left the loading bay at 6:10 a.m. but the driver, Ravi, has not scanned a single checkpoint since. The dispatcher says Ravi's phone is going straight to voicemail.\n\nYou open the AI assistant and type: 'Draft a short reply to Arjun explaining the delay and giving him an ETA.' The assistant returns this:\n\n### Details to use\n---\nHi Arjun,\nApologies for the inconvenience. Order #FC-2291 left our hub at 6:10 a.m. and is currently on its way to your site. Based on normal transit time, you can expect delivery by 10:00 a.m. Our team is actively tracking the consignment and will keep you updated.\nWarm regards,\nConnectCore Supply Chain\n---\n\nYour hub's standard transit time from dispatch to that Pune site is around 90 minutes — which is why 10:00 a.m. looks plausible on paper. But you have no GPS confirmation, no checkpoint scan, and no contact with the driver. You do not actually know where Ravi is.\n\n### Your response\nWrite what you would send to Arjun — and in one or two sentences, note what was wrong with the draft.",
          "title": "The assistant drafts a customer message with a promise you cannot keep",
