          "brief": "What would you write or record for this task?\n\n\n### The situation\nA customer emailed the Spicebox Kitchens feedback address last night. Her name is Meena. She says her home delivery order arrived 55 minutes late and the food was cold. She wants to know what Spicebox will do about it.\n\nRamesh asks you to draft a reply using the AI assistant before he reviews it. You type the situation into the assistant. It gives you this draft:\n\n---\nDear Meena,\n\nThank you for writing to us. We are extremely sorry for the delay and the cold food. As a valued customer, we will immediately arrange a full refund of your order to your original payment method within 24 hours, and we will also send you a complimentary meal voucher worth ₹500 by end of day today.\n\nThis will not happen again.\n\nWarm regards,\nSpicebox Kitchens\n---\n\n### Details to use\nYou check the Customer Complaints card pinned above the desk. It says:\n- Late delivery complaints: offer a 20% discount voucher on the next order. Refunds only if the order did not arrive at all.\n- Voucher values are ₹100 or ₹200. There is no ₹500 voucher.\n- Do not make promises about future service standards in writing.\n\nThe AI draft has three specific problems based on that card. Find all three, then write the corrected reply yourself.",
          "title": "The AI draft that promises too much",
          "answer": "artefact",
          "easier": "The student is told one of the three errors upfront and must find and fix the other two.",
          "fields": [
