          "brief": "What would you write or record for this task?\n\n\n### The situation\nIt is your thirtieth day at Swiftstore Logistics. Your manager Vikram has handed you a short project and said: 'Sort this out and tell me what you need.' He has not checked back.\n\nHere is what you have:\n\nA snapshot from this morning's inventory dashboard for five high-volume SKUs:\n\nSKU 2201 — System count: 80 — Physical count last week: 73 — Variance: -7\nSKU 3301 — System count: 45 — Physical count last week: 51 — Variance: +6\nSKU 4410 — System count: 120 — Physical count last week: 120 — Variance: 0\nSKU 7703 — System count: 4 — Physical count last week: 5 — Variance: +1\nSKU 8801 — System count: 33 — Physical count last week: 19 — Variance: -14\n\nSKU 8801 has the largest negative variance. It is also one of the most frequently dispatched items this month. Two pickers work the 8801 bay: Deepak (day shift) and Ravi (night shift).\n\n### Details to use\nPriya is not available today — she is at an off-site training. Write a one-page action plan (it can be in bullet points) covering:\n1. Which variance is most urgent and why.\n2. What you would do in the next 24 hours to find out what is causing it — be specific about who you would speak to, what records you would pull, and what you would check physically.\n3. How you would update the system records while the investigation is open — what status or flag you would apply, and why you would not just correct the count immediately.\n4. What you would tell Vikram when you hand this back to him — one short paragraph, plain language, no padding.",
          "title": "The stock audit nobody wants to own.",
          "answer": "artefact",
          "easier": "Vikram has told you the likely cause is a mis-scan at the pick station — your job is just to confirm it and close the record correctly.",
          "fields": [
            "Action plan: most urgent variance and reason",
