          "brief": "What would you write or record for this task?\n\n\n### The situation\nA customer, Meera Pillai, placed an order four days ago. The Swiftstore tracking system still shows her parcel as 'In Transit – Hub Delhi'. She has emailed twice asking where it is. Your team lead, Rakesh, has asked you to draft a reply before he gets out of his 10 a.m. meeting.\n\nYou open the AI assistant and type: 'Write a reply to a customer whose parcel has been stuck in transit for four days. Be apologetic and helpful.'\n\nThe assistant produces this draft:\n\n---\nDear Meera,\n\nThank you for reaching out to us. We sincerely apologise for the delay with your order. We have located your parcel and can confirm it will be delivered to you by tomorrow, 5 p.m. If it does not arrive by then, we will issue a full refund automatically.\n\nWe value your patience and assure you this will not happen again.\n\nWarm regards,\nSwiftstore Customer Support\n---\n\n### Details to use\nYou check the tracking system. It still says 'In Transit – Hub Delhi'. You have no update from the Delhi hub. You do not know when the parcel will move. Swiftstore's refund policy says a customer must raise a refund request themselves through the portal — refunds are never issued automatically.\n\nRewrite the email so it is honest, still warm, and does not make any promise the company cannot keep. Use Meera's name. Do not invent a delivery time. Do not promise an automatic refund. Tell her what she can actually do if the parcel does not arrive.",
          "title": "The Apology Email That Promises Too Much",
