          "brief": "Write the note to your manager.\n\n### The situation\nIt is the last day of your first month at FreshMart India. Your manager has left you this month's performance summary and a note: 'I've got a board call until noon. Look at this, figure out what needs attention, and leave me a short written note I can act on. Don't wait for me.'\n\nMonth summary — FreshMart India, Store #7:\n\n| Metric | This Month | Last Month | Target |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Total Revenue | ₹38,40,000 | ₹36,20,000 | ₹40,00,000 |\n| Footfall | 28,400 | 26,100 | 30,000 |\n| Conversion Rate | 71% | 74% | 78% |\n| Average Basket (₹) | 190 | 185 | 195 |\n| Waste as % of Stock | 4.8% | 3.9% | ≤3.5% |\n| Customer Complaints Logged | 38 | 21 | ≤25 |\n| Complaints Resolved Same Day | 24 of 38 | 19 of 21 | 90% |\n\n### Your response\nIt should: name the two metrics that need the most attention and why (use the numbers), suggest one concrete action for each, and flag any link you see between the metrics. Keep it under 200 words. Do not list every metric — choose.",
