          "brief": "What do you type into those two fields?\n\n### The situation\nYour floor manager has asked you to do a quick stock count for packaged atta (wheat flour) on Aisle 4 and update the store's inventory tracker — a shared Google Sheet where every row is one SKU, and the columns are: SKU name, system count (what the computer says is there), physical count (what you actually counted), and a notes column.\n\nYou count the shelf. There are 31 bags of Ashirvaad 5 kg atta. The system count says 45.\n\nKaran, who sits at the next workstation, tells you quietly: 'The last guy always just typed the system number in. Saves time, nobody really checks.'\n\nThe sheet is open in front of you. You need to fill in: physical count, and the notes column.\n\n### Your response\nThen, in one sentence below your answer, say why you did not type 45.",
          "title": "The count that does not match",
          "answer": "artefact",
          "easier": "Karan's comment is not in the scene — the student simply has a mismatched count and must decide what to record.",
