          "brief": "Write a discrepancy report.\n\n### The situation\nSwifthaul Logistics Pvt Ltd runs a small returns processing area where undelivered parcels are held before re-dispatch or disposal. Once a week, a coordinator does a stock check: they count what is physically in the bays and compare it to the system record.\n\nArjun did the count this morning and left you this note with the results. Your job is to go through it, spot every discrepancy, and write up a short discrepancy report that can be handed to the warehouse supervisor.\n\n**System record vs. physical count — Bay 3, 21 June:**\n\n### Details to use\n| Shelf Ref | Category              | System Count | Physical Count | Condition Note (Arjun's count) |\n|-----------|-----------------------|-------------|----------------|--------------------------------|\n| B3-01     | Undelivered – standard | 18          | 18             | All intact                     |\n| B3-02     | Undelivered – fragile  | 7           | 5              | 2 parcels missing, no record of removal |\n| B3-03     | Awaiting re-dispatch   | 24          | 24             | All intact                     |\n| B3-04     | Customer refused       | 11          | 14             | 3 extra parcels, no intake record found |\n| B3-05     | Damaged – hold         | 6           | 6              | All intact                     |\n| B3-06     | Awaiting disposal      | 9           | 4              | 5 parcels already removed, no disposal sign-off on file |\n\n### Your response\nIt should:\n1. List every shelf where the count does not match, with the exact difference.\n2. Note what is unusual or potentially serious about each one — not just that the numbers differ, but what might explain it or why it matters.\n3. Be factual and clear. The warehouse supervisor does not know you yet.",
          "image": "https://polkexjgphmwtpwhmspk.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/assessment-images/t1s011.png",
          "title": "The stock sheet does not match what is on the shelf",
          "answer": "artefact",
          "easier": "Reduce the table to four rows with only one discrepancy and ask the student to write just the section of the report covering that shelf.",
          "fields": [
            "Discrepancy report"
          ],
          "harder": "Tell the student that B3-06 parcels were scheduled for disposal last Wednesday and ask them to assess whether the removal was authorised or not, using only the information available.",
          "minutes": 4,
          "support": "assistant",
          "criteria": [
            "Identifies all three discrepancies: B3-02 (short by 2), B3-04 (over by 3), B3-06 (short by 5)",
            "Notes that B3-02 and B3-06 are potentially serious because there is no record of removal or sign-off — not just a count error",
            "Notes that B3-04's extra parcels with no intake record could indicate mis-shelving or an unlogged delivery",
            "Report is written in plain, factual language without guessing at fault or blaming anyone",
            "Reading data"
          ],
          "measures": [
            "Follow-through",
            "Clear communication",
            "Planning and organising"
          ],
