          "brief": "What would you write or record for this task?\n\n\n### The situation\nA customer named Arjun Mehta has sent this message to Shopnest India's support inbox:\n\n'Hi, I placed order #SN-87654 five days ago and paid for 2-day express delivery. It still hasn't arrived. I need it for an event this weekend. Please help.'\n\nPriya is at her desk. She says: 'Use the assistant to draft a reply — that's what it's there for. But read it before you send anything. We have had cases where the assistant promises things we cannot actually do.'\n\nThe operations policy sheet says:\n- Express delivery delays beyond 3 days qualify for a delivery fee refund only — not a product refund.\n- You cannot promise a delivery date. You can only say the team will investigate and provide an update within 4 business hours.\n- Always apologise and use the customer's name.\n\nThe assistant gives you this draft:\n\n---\nDear Arjun,\n\n### Details to use\nWe are very sorry for the inconvenience. Your order #SN-87654 will be delivered by tomorrow evening at the latest. We guarantee this. As a goodwill gesture, we will also refund the full product cost to your account within 24 hours.\n\nThank you for your patience.\nShopnest India Team\n---\n\nDo not send this draft. Fix it so it matches policy and actually helps Arjun. Write the corrected reply.",
