          "id": "t2s039",
          "day": "2",
          "team": "t2",
          "brief": "Edit the AI draft so it is accurate and honest, then type the final version of the reply you would actually send to Ritu.\n\n### The situation\nYou are on the operations desk, and your job today is to respond to escalated customer messages — ones that the frontline team has flagged as needing a more senior reply.\n\nA customer named Ritu Sharma wrote in forty minutes ago. Her order (Order #SNI-884201, a kurta set, ₹1,499) was supposed to arrive yesterday. The tracking system shows it is stuck at the Pune sorting hub since 6 a.m. — no movement since. She says this is a gift for her mother's birthday, which is tomorrow.\n\nYou open the AI assistant and type: 'Write a reply to a customer whose order is stuck at a sorting hub and has not moved in twelve hours. The order was supposed to arrive yesterday and is needed tomorrow as a birthday gift.'\n\nThe assistant produces this draft:\n\n---\nDear Ritu,\n\n### Details to use\nThank you for writing to us. We completely understand how important this delivery is, and we sincerely apologise for the delay.\n\nWe are pleased to confirm that your order will be delivered to you by tomorrow morning, 10 a.m. at the latest. Our logistics team has been alerted and will prioritise your shipment immediately.\n\nAs a goodwill gesture, we are also happy to offer you a full refund on your delivery charges.\n\nWarm regards,\nShopnest India Customer Operations\n---\n\nYou check the internal tracker. There is no option in the system to manually prioritise a shipment at a third-party sorting hub. The courier partner is Bluedart, and Shopnest has no direct line to the Pune hub — the escalation goes through a web portal and takes up to four hours for a response. You have no way to guarantee a 10 a.m. delivery tomorrow.\n\nYou also check the refund policy on the shared policy sheet pinned to the ops dashboard. It says: delivery charge refunds are approved only after a delay of more than 48 hours from the promised date. Ritu's order is currently 18 hours late.\n\n### Your response\nDo not just list what is wrong — write the real email.",
