          "id": "t2s040",
          "day": "3",
          "team": "t2",
          "brief": "Write the corrected priority order (1 to 5) that you will take into the standup.\n\n### The situation\nIt is day three. Every morning the operations coordinator pulls the exceptions list — orders that need a human decision today — and works through them in priority order.\n\nYou have ten minutes before the 9:30 standup with your team lead, Meera. You ask the AI assistant: 'I have five exceptions from this morning's tracker. Help me rank them by urgency so I can tell Meera what I am handling first.'\n\nYou paste in the following five rows from the tracker exactly as they appear:\n\n| Order ID     | Issue                          | Promise Date | Customer Tier | Hours Overdue |\n|--------------|-------------------------------|--------------|---------------|---------------|\n| SNI-991047   | Wrong item shipped             | 28 Apr       | Gold          | 36            |\n| SNI-990312   | Payment debited, order not created | 29 Apr  | Standard      | 4             |\n| SNI-991203   | Address undeliverable, courier holding | 29 Apr | Gold      | 5             |\n| SNI-989774   | Item out of stock after order confirmed | 27 Apr | Standard | 60           |\n| SNI-992801   | Customer claims non-delivery, tracker shows delivered | 29 Apr | Standard | 2 |\n\nToday's date is 29 April.\n\nThe AI assistant replies:\n\n---\nHere is your priority order for the standup:\n\n### Details to use\n1. SNI-991047 — Wrong item, Gold customer, 36 hours overdue. Highest urgency.\n2. SNI-991203 — Address issue, Gold customer, act before courier returns parcel.\n3. SNI-990312 — Payment taken, no order — financial issue, needs same-day fix.\n4. SNI-992801 — Non-delivery claim, low hours, can wait.\n5. SNI-989774 — Out of stock, 60 hours overdue — lowest urgency as stock issues resolve over time.\n---\n\nYou know from your induction that Shopnest's internal ops policy has two rules:\n- Any order where payment has been debited but no order record exists is a Tier-1 financial exception and must be the first call of the day, regardless of customer tier or hours.\n- An order that is 48 or more hours overdue with a Standard tier customer still outranks a same-day Gold issue on the exceptions list, because SLA breach penalties apply.\n\nThe AI has ranked the list using customer tier and hours overdue, but has ignored both of these rules.\n\n### Your response\nFor each item, write one sentence explaining why it sits where it does. You have ten minutes — keep it short and direct.",
