          "day": "1",
          "team": "t3",
          "brief": "What would you do in this situation?\n\n\n### The situation\nIt is your first morning at Brindavan Auto Components. Your manager, Priya, has sat you down at the operations desk and shown you the daily dispatch board — a printed sheet pinned to the board beside your screen that the outbound team fills in each morning. She says: 'One thing you will do every day is check this against the system before 10 a.m. and flag anything that looks off. Have a look at today's.' She points to the sheet and leaves for a meeting.\n\nThe dispatch board shows the following for today, 14 July:\n\n### Details to use\n| Order ID | Customer | Units Dispatched | Carrier | Status |\n|----------|----------|-----------------|---------|--------|\n| ORD-2201 | Mahindra Chennai | 240 | BlueDart | Dispatched |\n| ORD-2202 | Tata Motors Pune | 180 | DTDC | Dispatched |\n| ORD-2203 | Hero MotoCorp Delhi | 300 | BlueDart | Dispatched |\n| ORD-2204 | Maruti Suzuki Gurgaon | 150 | DTDC | Pending |\n| ORD-2205 | Mahindra Chennai | 240 | BlueDart | Dispatched |\n\nYou then open the operations system on your screen. The system's dispatch log for today shows:\n\n| Order ID | Units Logged | Carrier Confirmed |\n|----------|-------------|-------------------|\n| ORD-2201 | 240 | BlueDart |\n| ORD-2202 | 180 | DTDC |\n| ORD-2203 | 300 | BlueDart |\n| ORD-2204 | 150 | Not confirmed |\n| ORD-2205 | 120 | BlueDart |\n\nPriya will be back in ten minutes. She will ask: 'Did you find anything?' Write what you will tell her — which order has a problem, what the problem is, and what you think should happen next.",
          "title": "The dispatch board does not add up",
          "answer": "typed",
          "easier": "Tell Priya only which order has the discrepancy and what the two different numbers are.",
          "fields": [],
          "harder": "Write a short message Priya could forward to the outbound team asking them to confirm the correct figure before the 10 a.m. cutoff, without making it sound like an accusation.",
          "minutes": 3,
          "support": "assistant",
          "criteria": [
            "Identifies ORD-2205 specifically — the board says 240 units but the system shows 120",
            "States clearly that the two sources disagree, not just that a number looks wrong",
            "Suggests a next step — checking with the outbound team or the carrier — rather than stopping at the observation",
            "Does not mix up ORD-2204, which is a separate pending status issue, with the unit count discrepancy",
            "Reading data"
          ],
          "measures": [
            "Clear communication",
            "Problem solving"
          ],
          "needsImage": false
