          "id": "t3s048",
          "day": "2",
          "team": "t3",
          "brief": "Fill in the ticket.\n\n### The situation\nOn your second day, the stores team hands you a goods-received note (GRN) — a form they fill in whenever a supplier delivery arrives. Suresh, the colleague at the next desk, explains: 'Every GRN should match the purchase order in the system. If it does not, you raise a short-supply ticket so procurement knows to chase the supplier. Have a look at this morning's.'\n\nThe GRN for today's delivery from Kothari Pressings reads:\n\n| Part Number | Part Name | PO Quantity | Quantity Received | Condition |\n|-------------|-----------|-------------|-------------------|----------|\n| KP-0041 | Bracket Assy – Front | 500 | 500 | Good |\n| KP-0042 | Bracket Assy – Rear | 500 | 480 | Good |\n| KP-0043 | Hinge Pin Set | 1000 | 1000 | Good |\n| KP-0044 | Mounting Plate | 300 | 300 | Good |\n| KP-0045 | Clip Set – Door | 800 | 800 | Damaged – 40 units |\n\n### Details to use\nThe purchase order in the system confirms these quantities: KP-0041: 500, KP-0042: 500, KP-0043: 1000, KP-0044: 300, KP-0045: 800.\n\nYou need to raise a short-supply ticket in the tracker. The ticket form has these fields: Supplier name, Part number(s) affected, Description of issue, Quantity short or damaged, Suggested action.\n\n### Your response\nThere are two issues in this GRN — make sure your ticket covers both.",
          "title": "A supplier's delivery looks short",
          "answer": "artefact",
          "easier": "Fill in the ticket for KP-0042 only, the short delivery.",
          "fields": [
            "Supplier name",
            "Part number(s) affected",
            "Description of issue",
            "Quantity short or damaged",
            "Suggested action"
          ],
          "harder": "After filling in the ticket, write a one-paragraph note to procurement explaining the combined impact so they can decide whether to hold the production line for KP-0042 or source from elsewhere.",
          "minutes": 4,
          "support": "assistant",
          "criteria": [
            "Raises the ticket for both KP-0042 (20 units short) and KP-0045 (40 units damaged) — missing either one is incomplete",
            "States the correct shortfall numbers: 20 for KP-0042 and 40 for KP-0045",
            "Distinguishes between a quantity shortfall and a damage issue rather than labelling both the same way",
            "Suggests a specific action — such as requesting re-delivery or credit note — for at least one of the two issues",
            "Reading data"
