          "id": "t3s049",
          "day": "3",
          "team": "t3",
          "brief": "What would you do in this situation?\n\n\n### The situation\nEach shift at Brindavan Auto Components ends with the line supervisor filling in an output sheet showing how many units each line produced. Your manager Priya has asked you to compare today's morning-shift output sheet against the production plan and report back by lunch.\n\nThe production plan for the morning shift (6 a.m.–2 p.m.) targets:\n- Line A: 600 units of Part BV-11\n- Line B: 450 units of Part BV-22\n- Line C: 300 units of Part BV-33\n- Line D: 200 units of Part BV-44\n\nThe output sheet the supervisor handed in shows:\n- Line A: 610 units of BV-11 — shift ran smoothly\n- Line B: 390 units of BV-22 — machine stoppage 45 min\n- Line C: 300 units of BV-33 — no issues\n- Line D: no entry\n\nYou use it to draft the summary you will send Priya. The assistant produces this draft:\n\n### Details to use\n'Morning shift summary: Line A exceeded target by 10 units. Line B fell short by 50 units due to machine stoppage. Line C met target. Line D met target with 200 units produced.'\n\nBefore you send it, read the draft carefully against the output sheet. There is something wrong with it. Fix the draft so it is accurate, then send the corrected version to Priya.",
          "title": "The production line output sheet has a gap",
          "answer": "typed",
          "easier": "Just identify the one thing the assistant got wrong and say in one sentence what the correct version should say.",
          "fields": [],
          "harder": "Add a line to the corrected summary recommending a specific action — who should be contacted and by when — to get Line D's data before end of day.",
          "minutes": 3,
          "support": "assistant",
          "criteria": [
            "Catches that Line D has no entry on the output sheet — the assistant's claim that Line D met target is invented",
            "Corrects the draft to say Line D has no data submitted, not that it met target",
            "Keeps the accurate parts of the draft — Lines A, B and C — intact rather than rewriting everything",
            "The final message is something Priya can act on: it is clear, brief, and flags that Line D needs follow-up",
            "Reading data"
          ],
          "measures": [
            "Clear communication",
            "Problem solving"
          ],
          "needsImage": false
