          "id": "t3s050",
          "day": "7",
          "team": "t3",
          "brief": "Write two things: first, a short internal note to add to the overdue ticket explaining that it is past due and what you are doing about it.\n\n### The situation\nYou are now managing the operations ticket tracker at Brindavan Auto Components. The tracker lists every open issue that needs action. This morning you open it and see the following:\n\n| Ticket ID | Issue | Raised On | Due Date | Assigned To | Status |\n|-----------|-------|-----------|----------|-------------|--------|\n| OPS-114 | Short delivery – Kothari Pressings KP-0042 | 10 Jul | 14 Jul | Procurement – Rajan | Open |\n| OPS-117 | Machine stoppage – Line B, BV-22 | 12 Jul | 15 Jul | Maintenance – Anand | In Progress |\n| OPS-119 | Customer query – Maruti Suzuki order delay | 13 Jul | 15 Jul | You | Open |\n| OPS-121 | Damaged goods – KP-0045 clip sets | 13 Jul | 17 Jul | Procurement – Rajan | Open |\n\nToday is 15 July.\n\n### Details to use\nLook at the tracker carefully. One ticket is already past its due date and still open. One ticket assigned to you has no update recorded against it.\n\nYou cannot reach Rajan right now — he is in the factory floor. Suresh is at his desk.\n\n### Your response\nSecond, a reply to the Maruti Suzuki customer — their query is about an order delay and you do not yet have the full answer, but you want them to know someone is looking into it.",
          "title": "Three open tickets, one is overdue",
          "answer": "typed",
          "easier": "Write only the internal note for the overdue ticket, not the customer reply.",
          "fields": [],
          "harder": "After writing both, add a priority order for all four tickets today with one sentence explaining your reasoning.",
          "minutes": 4,
          "support": "assistant",
          "criteria": [
            "Correctly identifies OPS-114 as the overdue ticket — due 14 July, still open on 15 July",
            "The internal note states the ticket is overdue, acknowledges Rajan is unreachable, and names a concrete next step",
            "The customer reply does not promise a delivery date that has not been confirmed",
            "The customer reply is professional and reassuring without being vague — it tells Maruti Suzuki what will happen next and by when"
          ],
          "measures": [
            "Follow-through",
            "Customer care",
