          "id": "t3s051",
          "day": "14",
          "team": "t3",
          "brief": "What would you say in this situation?\n\n\n### The situation\nEvery Monday you compile the weekly production output report for your manager Priya using data from the line supervisors. This is Week 28 (7–12 July). The supervisors have sent you their daily totals and you have put them into the report. Before you send it, Priya has told you to always sanity-check it yourself first.\n\nHere is the compiled report:\n\n| Line | Mon | Tue | Wed | Thu | Fri | Sat | Weekly Total |\n|------|-----|-----|-----|-----|-----|-----|-------------|\n| Line A (BV-11) | 620 | 615 | 608 | 611 | 619 | 600 | 3,673 |\n| Line B (BV-22) | 460 | 455 | 448 | 450 | 462 | 440 | 2,715 |\n| Line C (BV-33) | 305 | 300 | 298 | 302 | 299 | 295 | 1,799 |\n| Line D (BV-44) | 210 | 208 | 940 | 205 | 211 | 200 | 1,974 |\n\nThe weekly plan targets are: Line A: 3,600 units, Line B: 2,700 units, Line C: 1,800 units, Line D: 1,200 units.\n\n### Details to use\nNote: Line D runs a single shift and its daily output should not exceed 215 units on any day. The factory does not run double shifts on weekdays.\n\nSpend two minutes looking at this data. Something in it is clearly wrong — not a small rounding difference, but a number that cannot be right given what you know about the line. Write a spoken response (you will say this out loud as if Priya has just asked you 'Anything odd in the report before I send it up?'). Say what you found, why it cannot be right, and what you want to do before the report goes out.",
          "title": "The weekly output report has a line that does not fit",
          "answer": "spoken",
          "easier": "Just say which cell is wrong and what a plausible correct number would look like.",
          "fields": [],
          "harder": "Also calculate what Line D's weekly total would be if Wednesday were corrected to a typical value, and say whether the line met its 1,200-unit plan target that week.",
          "minutes": 3,
          "support": "assistant",
          "criteria": [
            "Identifies Wednesday's Line D figure of 940 as the error — more than four times a normal day's output",
            "References the constraint that Line D cannot exceed 215 units in a single shift to explain why 940 is impossible",
            "Notes that the weekly total for Line D is therefore also wrong",
            "States clearly what they will do — verify with the Line D supervisor — before allowing the report to go out",
            "Reading data"
          ],
          "measures": [
            "Clear communication",
            "Composure under pressure",
            "Follow-through"
