          "team": "t3",
          "brief": "What would you do in this situation?\n\n\n### The situation\nIt is the end of your first month. Priya hands you a task with no further instructions: 'Sort out next week's dispatch plan given the parts situation. Come back to me with what you're recommending and what you need from me.'\n\nHere is what you have:\n\n**Confirmed customer orders for next week (18–22 July):**\n| Order ID | Customer | Part | Units Ordered | Committed Dispatch Date |\n|----------|----------|------|---------------|------------------------|\n| ORD-2310 | Tata Motors Pune | BV-11 | 600 | 18 Jul |\n| ORD-2311 | Maruti Suzuki Gurgaon | BV-22 | 400 | 19 Jul |\n| ORD-2312 | Mahindra Chennai | BV-11 | 350 | 20 Jul |\n| ORD-2313 | Hero MotoCorp Delhi | BV-33 | 300 | 21 Jul |\n| ORD-2314 | Tata Motors Pune | BV-22 | 200 | 22 Jul |\n\n**Current finished goods stock (end of this week):**\n- BV-11: 820 units\n- BV-22: 390 units\n- BV-33: 300 units\n\n### Details to use\n**Production plan for next week (before adjustment):**\n- Line A makes 600 BV-11 units across the week\n- Line B makes 450 BV-22 units across the week\n- Line C makes 300 BV-33 units across the week\n\n**Problem just confirmed:** Kothari Pressings cannot deliver the raw material for BV-22 until 20 July at the earliest. Line B cannot start production until material arrives. BV-22 stock on hand is 390 units.\n\nWork out whether the BV-22 orders can be fulfilled on their committed dates. Write your recommendation to Priya: what you can deliver on time, what you cannot, what options you see, and one specific thing you need her to decide or approve.",
