          "day": "3",
          "team": "t3",
          "brief": "What would you do in this situation?\n\n\n### The situation\nYou are covering the operations inbox while Suresh is at his desk beside you.\n\nAn email comes in from the quality team at 9:04 am: 'Batch #QC-229 (crankshaft covers, 150 units) has been put on hold pending re-inspection.\n\nDo not dispatch.' You check the production tracker — the shared system where every batch has a row — and Batch #QC-229 is still showing Status: 'Ready for Dispatch', with no hold noted anywhere.\n\nThe dispatch team works from this tracker.\n\nIf they pull the list at 11 am and see 'Ready for Dispatch', the batch could go out.\n\nYou could forward the email to the dispatch supervisor and leave the tracker as it is, on the grounds that updating the tracker is not technically your job on day three and you do not want to touch something you might get wrong.\n\nOr you can update it.\n\n### Details to use\nThe tracker fields for this row are: Status, Hold Reason, Hold Logged By, and Hold Logged At.\n\nType what you would enter in each tracker field and write a short Notes entry explaining the hold.\n\nCheck it against the quality email and explain why dispatch must wait.",
