          "team": "t3",
          "brief": "What would you do in this situation?\n\n\n### The situation\nEvery morning at Brindavan Auto Components, the operations team checks the inbound stock dashboard before the 9 am production meeting. Today's dashboard shows a single row that concerns you:\n\nPO# BAC-IN-302 | Supplier: Yamuna Forgings | Item: Connecting rod blanks | Expected Qty: 500 | Received Qty (system): 500 | Status: Complete\n\nThe system says all 500 arrived.\n\nBut you walk past Bay 3 on your way in and count only four stacked pallets.\n\nEach pallet holds 80 units.\n\nThat is 320 units, not 500.\n\nThe goods receipt note clipped to the bay wall is signed by the stores clerk, Vimal, and dated yesterday.\n\nThe 9 am meeting is in twenty minutes.\n\nSuresh is at his desk.\n\nThe quick thing to do is say nothing — the system says Complete, the meeting will move on, and maybe you miscounted.\n\n### Your response\nWrite: (1) what the dashboard row actually tells you versus what you observed at the bay, (2) what you would do in the next twenty minutes before the meeting, and (3) how you would record the discrepancy in the system — specifically what fields you would flag and what you would write — even if you cannot get it fully resolved before the meeting starts.",
          "image": "https://polkexjgphmwtpwhmspk.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/assessment-images/t3s056.png",
          "title": "The Dashboard Row That Does Not Match the Bay",
          "answer": "typed",
