          "id": "t3s059",
          "day": "2",
          "team": "t3",
          "brief": "Write the corrected version of this email — the one you would put in front of Deepa for approval.\n\n### The situation\nYou coordinate daily operations — which means when something goes wrong on the floor, you are the one who writes to the customer.\n\nThis morning, Batch 447 of rear-bracket assemblies missed its dispatch window. The production supervisor has told you the delay is two days: the parts will be ready by end of Thursday, not Tuesday as originally confirmed. The customer is Raj Motors, and their purchase order reference is RM-2291.\n\nYour manager, Deepa, has asked you to draft an apology email to the buyer at Raj Motors, a Mr Arvind Nair. She is in a supplier review meeting until noon and has told you to use the AI assistant to get a draft out quickly — she will approve it before it goes.\n\nYou open the assistant and type: \"Draft an apology email to a customer. Our batch is delayed by two days. Be professional and reassuring.\"\n\n### Details to use\nThe assistant returns this:\n\n---\nSubject: Update on Your Order – Batch 447\n\nDear Mr Nair,\n\nThank you for your continued partnership with Brindavan Auto Components. We sincerely apologise for the delay to Batch 447 against your purchase order RM-2291. Due to an unforeseen production issue, dispatch has been pushed back by two days to Thursday. We assure you this is a one-off situation.\n\nTo make up for the inconvenience, we will arrange express courier at no extra charge and ensure delivery reaches you by Friday morning.\n\nPlease be assured this will not affect any future orders. We value your relationship and will keep you updated.\n\nWarm regards,\nOperations Team\nBrindavan Auto Components\n---\n\nRead the draft carefully. You have not spoken to the logistics team about courier options. Nobody has told you express delivery is available or approved for this order. You do not know if Friday morning delivery is actually possible.\n\n### Your response\nFix what the AI got wrong. Keep what it got right. Do not add promises you cannot back up.",
          "title": "The AI draft promises something we cannot keep",
          "answer": "artefact",
          "easier": "The assistant's draft only contains one problem: the Friday morning delivery promise. Remove that one line and adjust the email.",
