          "brief": "Write the Action Taken entry for this row.\n\n### The situation\nThe Operations Coordinator who was here before you left a handover note on your desk. It says: 'The welcome desk log is the main thing you'll touch every day. Every patient complaint, every request, every escalation gets written in there so the next shift knows what's outstanding. Nothing verbal, nothing on paper only — if it's not in the log, it didn't happen.'\n\nNandini, the colleague at the next desk, has just shown you where the log is. It is a shared online form. Each row has four columns: Date/Time, Issue, Action Taken, Status (Open / Closed).\n\nRight now there is one incomplete row sitting in the log from yesterday evening:\n- Date/Time: 14 May, 6:45 pm\n- Issue: Patient in Ward 3B says her discharge summary was not given to her before she left. She called in from home.\n- Action Taken: [blank]\n- Status: Open\n\n### Details to use\nNandini tells you: 'Nobody filled in what happened next. Before you do anything else, write what should go in the Action Taken column based on what we actually know — which is only what's in this row. Don't invent steps that didn't happen. Just record what the situation is so the next person can pick it up cleanly.'\n\n### Your response\nKeep it to two or three sentences.",
