          "brief": "Draft a short message (three to five sentences) to the OT Manager, Dr Ramesh Iyer, flagging OT-4.\n\n### The situation\nAt Meditrust Hospitals, the operations team reviews the previous day's Operating Theatre (OT) utilisation dashboard each morning. Nandini has pulled it up for you and said, 'Have a read, tell me what stands out. We report anything below 70% to the OT Manager by 9:30 a.m.'\n\nYesterday's dashboard:\n\nOT Suite | Scheduled procedures | Completed procedures | Cancellations | Utilisation %\nOT-1 | 8 | 7 | 1 | 87%\nOT-2 | 6 | 6 | 0 | 100%\nOT-3 | 7 | 5 | 2 | 71%\nOT-4 | 6 | 2 | 4 | 33%\nOT-5 | 5 | 5 | 0 | 100%\n\nLook at the data. OT-4 has four cancellations — the highest of any suite — and a utilisation rate of 33%. Every other suite is at 71% or above. Something caused four procedures in one suite to be cancelled, and that is outside normal variation.\n\n### Your response\nState the specific numbers, say you do not yet know the reason, and ask whether he wants operations to follow up or whether his team is already looking into it.",
          "title": "Daily OT utilisation dashboard — one number that does not fit",
          "answer": "typed",
          "easier": "Add a note in the brief: 'Anything with 3 or more cancellations needs to be flagged regardless of utilisation percentage.'",
          "fields": [],
          "harder": "Remove the utilisation % column so the student must calculate it themselves (completed ÷ scheduled) before deciding what to flag.",
          "minutes": 4,
          "support": "assistant",
          "criteria": [
