          "id": "t4s072",
          "day": "30",
          "team": "t4",
          "brief": "Write the one-page summary for Ms Kavitha Suresh.\n\n### The situation\nIt is day thirty. Your manager, Ms Kavitha Suresh, has sent you the following message this morning:\n\n'I need you to review last month's operations exception log and send me a one-page summary by 3 p.m. Flag what is recurring, what is one-off, and what needs a fix. Nobody will check your work before it goes to her — you decide what to put in it.'\n\nThe exception log for the month:\n\nDate | Type | Description | Resolved?\n02-Jun | Discharge delay | Transport not booked — P-108.\n\nBed held 4 hours extra. | Yes\n05-Jun | Equipment | OT-4 suction unit failure — 2 procedures delayed. | Yes\n07-Jun | Discharge delay | Transport not booked — P-134.\n\n### Details to use\nBed held 6 hours extra. | Yes\n09-Jun | Stock | Sodium Chloride IV bags below minimum — replenishment raised same day. | Yes\n12-Jun | Equipment | Ward B drip stand broken — replaced next day. | Yes\n14-Jun | Discharge delay | Transport not booked — P-156.\n\nBed held 3 hours extra. | Yes\n18-Jun | Stock | Azithromycin below minimum — not flagged by system, raised manually. | Yes\n21-Jun | Complaint | Family of patient P-201 unhappy with wait time at discharge. | Yes\n24-Jun | Discharge delay | Transport not booked — P-189.\n\nBed held 5 hours extra. | Yes\n28-Jun | Equipment | OT-2 light fitting flickering — maintenance called. | Yes\n\nAll exceptions show as resolved. But the transport-not-booked discharge delay appears four times across the month — 2 Jun, 7 Jun, 14 Jun, 24 Jun — and the bed hold times are 4, 6, 3 and 5 hours. That is a pattern, not a one-off, and the fact that each is marked 'resolved' does not mean the root cause has been fixed.\n\n### Your response\nIt must: name the recurring issue clearly, include the specific dates and bed-hold hours, distinguish it from the one-off exceptions, and recommend one concrete operational change. You choose the recommendation — own it.",
          "title": "End-of-month operations summary — spot the pattern and own the follow-up",
          "answer": "artefact",
          "easier": "Add a column to the log called 'Recurring?' with 'Yes' marked against the four transport entries.",
          "fields": [
            "One-page summary for Ms Kavitha Suresh"
