          "team": "t4",
          "brief": "Write the updated note for ticket OD-1901.\n\n### The situation\nMeditrust Hospitals runs two tools side by side: OpsDesk (the service-ticket system) and MedStore (the inventory tracker for consumables). They are supposed to agree with each other.\n\nThe Radiology department has raised a verbal complaint that they are low on contrast-media syringes. You check MedStore and it shows:\n\nItem: Contrast-media syringe 50ml\nStock on hand: 38 units\nLast updated: 6 days ago\n\nYou then open OpsDesk and find:\n\nTicket #OD-1901 (raised 3 days ago)\nRequest: Urgent restock — contrast-media syringes, Radiology\nStatus: IN PROGRESS\nNote: 'Store confirmed 38 units available. No restock needed. Monitoring.'\n\nSo the ticket was half-closed on the basis of a MedStore number that is now six days old. You do not know the real current count. Radiology is still complaining.\n\n### Details to use\nYou cannot update MedStore yourself — only the stores team can do a physical count and enter it. But you can update the OpsDesk ticket right now.\n\n### Your response\nIt should record what the discrepancy is, what you have not yet confirmed, and what action you are requesting from the stores team. Do not mark the ticket resolved or closed.",
          "title": "Two Systems, Two Different Answers",
          "answer": "artefact",
          "easier": "Nandini has already drafted a note you can review and adjust before submitting.",
          "fields": [
