          "team": "t4",
          "brief": "Fix the draft and send the corrected version.\n\n### The situation\nYou are handling a complaint from a patient's family. Mr. Arvind Shenoy contacted the hospital's operations helpline because his mother's discharge paperwork was not ready when she was supposed to leave this morning. She waited in the discharge lounge for over two hours.\n\nYou have looked into it: the delay was caused by a pharmacy sign-off that was missed in the system. The paperwork is now ready. You need to send Mr. Shenoy a short apology email and confirm he can collect the documents.\n\nYou open the AI assistant and type: 'Write an apology email to a patient's family member whose mother's discharge paperwork was delayed by two hours due to a pharmacy sign-off issue. Tell him the documents are ready and he can collect them.'\n\nThe assistant returns this draft:\n\n---\nDear Mr. Shenoy,\n\n### Details to use\nWe sincerely apologise for the inconvenience caused this morning. Due to a pharmacy sign-off delay, your mother's discharge paperwork was not ready on time. We understand how distressing this must have been.\n\nWe are pleased to confirm that all documents are now ready for collection at the Discharge Desk, which is open 24 hours a day. You may collect them at any time before 6:00 pm today.\n\n---\n\nThere are two problems in this draft. The Discharge Desk is not open 24 hours — it closes at 8:00 pm. And the 6:00 pm deadline is something the AI invented; no such cutoff exists. If Mr. Shenoy reads both sentences, they contradict each other, and either way the AI has put a time limit on something you never told it.\n\n### Your response\nThe only confirmed fact is that the documents are ready now. Do not add any time you have not verified.",
