          "brief": "What would you do in this situation?\n\n\n### The situation\nIt is 11 am. The facilities manager, Rajesh, stops by your desk and tells you verbally that he escalated a linen-supply issue on Ward 3 to the linen vendor yesterday afternoon — the vendor has agreed to send an emergency delivery by 3 pm today.\n\nYou open OpsDesk and find the related ticket:\n\nTicket #OD-1923\nRaised by: Ward 3 Nursing Station\nRequest: Linen shortage — beds cannot be made up for incoming patients\nStatus: IN PROGRESS\nLast note (3 days ago): 'Flagged to facilities team. Awaiting response.'\n\nNothing in the system reflects what Rajesh just told you. No escalation note. No vendor name. No expected delivery time. If Rajesh is in a meeting at 3 pm and the delivery does not arrive, whoever picks this up will see 'Awaiting response' and not know an escalation happened at all.\n\n### Details to use\nRajesh has already walked away. You cannot ask him to log it himself right now.\n\nUpdate ticket OD-1923 so the record reflects what you were just told. Write the note you would add. Then, in one sentence below the note, explain why you are logging someone else's verbal update rather than waiting for them to do it themselves.",
