          "brief": "Correct the draft and write the version you would actually send.\n\n### The situation\nIt is 8:10 AM. You are covering the morning ops check at Meditrust Hospitals. The on-duty nurse, Sister Priya, has just called to say that the Operation Theatre 2 schedule for today shows a 90-minute unallocated slot between 11:00 AM and 12:30 PM — the surgeon who was booked, Dr. Mahesh Rao, has called in sick.\n\nYour job right now is to send a brief internal alert to the OT Scheduling team (scheduling@meditrust.in) so they can reassign or fill the slot. You do not make the reassignment yourself — that is the scheduling team's call.\n\nYou open the AI assistant and ask it to draft the alert. It produces this:\n\n---\n\"Subject: OT 2 Slot Vacant — Immediate Attention Required\n\nDear Team,\n\n### Details to use\nPlease note that Operation Theatre 2 has an unallocated slot today from 11:00 AM to 1:30 PM due to Dr. Mahesh Rao being unavailable. This is a 2.5-hour window. Please arrange for reassignment at the earliest.\n\nRegards,\nOperations Coordinator\"\n---\n\nRead the draft carefully before you send it. Sister Priya told you the slot is 11:00 AM to 12:30 PM — that is 90 minutes, not two and a half hours. The AI has written 1:30 PM and called it a 2.5-hour window. Both figures are wrong.\n\n### Your response\nDo not change anything else about the tone or structure unless you feel it needs it. In a note below the draft, write one sentence explaining what was wrong in the AI's version and why it mattered to fix it before sending.",
