          "brief": "Write the reply you would actually send.\n\n### The situation\nA customer named Rahul Mehta ordered a birthday cake topper (Order #SN-88321) for his daughter's party on Saturday. It is now Friday afternoon and the tracker still shows 'Out for delivery' since 9 a.m. He has written in saying: 'This is a joke. I needed this today. If it doesn't arrive in two hours I want a full refund AND you to pay for a replacement I buy locally.' You open the AI assistant and paste his message in. It drafts this reply:\n\n'Dear Rahul, we sincerely apologise for the delay. Your order is expected by 6 p.m. today. As a goodwill gesture we are happy to offer a full refund plus ₹500 store credit, which will appear in your Shopnest wallet within 24 hours.'\n\n### Details to use\nThere are two problems with this draft before you can send it. First, the tracker has not given you any confirmed 6 p.m. estimate — that figure came from nowhere. Second, Shopnest India's standard goodwill credit for a delayed order under ₹999 is ₹200, not ₹500 (you checked the policy sheet Priya shared with you on Day 2). Priya is away from her desk. You need to send a reply to Rahul within the next ten minutes.\n\n### Your response\nThen, in two or three sentences below it, explain what was wrong with the AI draft and what you changed.",
          "title": "Fix the AI's apology before it goes out",
          "answer": "artefact",
          "easier": "Tell the student in advance that the draft contains exactly two factual errors and ask them to find and fix both.",
